1
00:00:01,334 --> 00:00:02,376
"Previously on The Mentalist..."

2
00:00:02,502 --> 00:00:03,794
"I can't do this anymore."

3
00:00:03,920 --> 00:00:06,923
You can't keep pulling me
from the path of oncoming trains.

4
00:00:07,048 --> 00:00:09,091
There's new trains coming
every day.

5
00:00:09,342 --> 00:00:10,718
You have information
about the case?

6
00:00:10,843 --> 00:00:12,970
My brother does. Gabriel.
He's a psychic.

7
00:00:13,095 --> 00:00:14,597
There's a thing inside you.

8
00:00:15,306 --> 00:00:17,099
"Your cure will come
with the number three."

9
00:00:18,559 --> 00:00:19,852
I didn't know where you were.

10
00:00:19,977 --> 00:00:22,063
- You knew I'd be back.
- No, I didn't.

11
00:00:22,271 --> 00:00:23,481
There's a serial killer

12
00:00:23,606 --> 00:00:25,900
"with an evil heart
and an appetite to kill."

13
00:00:26,067 --> 00:00:28,569
I saw that the killer
is going to kill again. Tonight.

14
00:00:30,279 --> 00:00:32,823
"Why would the killer care
if Gabriel was a real psychic?"

15
00:00:32,949 --> 00:00:35,993
"He wants one for some reason
and Gabriel didn't pass the test."

16
00:00:38,204 --> 00:00:40,831
- "Could you just take a look?"
- "He was sitting in the car, right?"

17
00:00:40,998 --> 00:00:42,833
The whole time I was putting out
the trash

18
00:00:42,959 --> 00:00:45,378
he just sat there, staring at me.

19
00:00:45,545 --> 00:00:47,672
They still haven't caught that guy
who killed those people.

20
00:00:48,089 --> 00:00:49,507
It could be him. You don't know.

21
00:00:50,341 --> 00:00:53,928
Serial killers don't sit in cars.
They lurk in the shadows.

22
00:00:55,388 --> 00:00:56,430
Be right back.

23
00:01:34,594 --> 00:01:35,636
Hey.

24
00:01:45,605 --> 00:01:46,647
Stupid drunk.

25
00:01:51,444 --> 00:01:52,486
Oh!

26
00:01:55,406 --> 00:01:56,449
Susan!

27
00:02:02,830 --> 00:02:03,873
Soos?

28
00:02:17,803 --> 00:02:18,846
Soos?

29
00:02:24,101 --> 00:02:25,144
"What is this?"

30
00:02:25,603 --> 00:02:26,646
Did you buy me another horse?

31
00:02:28,105 --> 00:02:29,607
- Just a little further.
- Okay.

32
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:32,443
Is this a trick?

33
00:02:32,777 --> 00:02:36,072
- Breathe that air in.
- Okay, I'm breathing in that air.

34
00:02:36,197 --> 00:02:37,948
And... voilà.

35
00:02:41,577 --> 00:02:43,621
Jane... what is this?

36
00:02:44,330 --> 00:02:47,500
It's a little shack that I'm gonna renovate
make some additions.

37
00:02:47,875 --> 00:02:49,377
We both knew things had to change.

38
00:02:49,502 --> 00:02:53,547
I-I couldn't make you quit,
and I need something to do.

39
00:02:53,964 --> 00:02:55,966
- So you're gonna build us a house.
- That's right.

40
00:02:56,092 --> 00:02:57,968
And when I'm done, if nothing else

41
00:02:58,344 --> 00:02:59,512
we have a place to live.

42
00:03:00,346 --> 00:03:01,389
It's a start.

43
00:03:01,597 --> 00:03:03,683
So you're gonna work here, not...
not at the FBI.

44
00:03:03,808 --> 00:03:05,643
- You're quitting.
- Maybe. I-I don't know.

45
00:03:05,768 --> 00:03:06,852
I haven't decided yet.

46
00:03:10,189 --> 00:03:11,232
What?

47
00:03:13,150 --> 00:03:15,945
I'm glad you got it. I am.
But...

48
00:03:16,779 --> 00:03:17,822
I have needs, too.

49
00:03:19,198 --> 00:03:20,241
Like what?

50
00:03:21,784 --> 00:03:23,619
I need to know
that you're not gonna run away again.

51
00:03:23,744 --> 00:03:24,787
I won't.

52
00:03:24,912 --> 00:03:27,039
I need to know
that you're committed to this, to us.

53
00:03:27,373 --> 00:03:29,458
I-I am. That's why I wanna do this.

54
00:03:32,503 --> 00:03:33,546
Okay.

55
00:03:34,672 --> 00:03:36,340
Then are you gonna take off
your wedding ring?

56
00:03:38,134 --> 00:03:40,803
It just, it seems like
you don't wanna let go of it.

57
00:03:41,178 --> 00:03:44,890
- No, it's not that.
- I-I understand why it's difficult for you.

58
00:03:45,015 --> 00:03:47,518
- It-it's just that I'm used to it.
- I know. It...

59
00:03:54,483 --> 00:03:55,526
What's up, boss?

60
00:03:55,651 --> 00:03:57,570
"Sorry, Lisbon.
I know you're on your way home."

61
00:03:57,695 --> 00:03:58,779
"But I need you to turn around."

62
00:03:59,405 --> 00:04:00,448
We have another one.

63
00:04:16,670 --> 00:04:18,380
The victim's name is Susan Herman.

64
00:04:18,964 --> 00:04:21,425
Her husband reported her
missing last night.

65
00:04:22,050 --> 00:04:24,094
Apparently, the killer snatched
her off her porch.

66
00:04:24,219 --> 00:04:26,430
- That's a change.
- The pattern's the same otherwise...

67
00:04:26,555 --> 00:04:28,557
Shot in the chest,
one fingernail ripped off.

68
00:04:28,682 --> 00:04:29,933
He didn't bother hiding the body.

69
00:04:30,267 --> 00:04:31,310
Could mean he's getting bolder.

70
00:04:31,602 --> 00:04:32,728
Or more playful.

71
00:04:33,187 --> 00:04:34,480
- Playful?
- Well, sure.

72
00:04:34,938 --> 00:04:37,232
{\an8}He knows we're on to him.
That's why he left her out for us to find.

73
00:04:37,357 --> 00:04:39,318
{\an8}- He's also done something else.
- What?

74
00:04:40,152 --> 00:04:41,195
I'm not sure.

75
00:04:41,820 --> 00:04:42,863
Uh, excuse me.

76
00:04:43,155 --> 00:04:45,949
{\an8}That mark on her left arm...
is that a puncture wound?

77
00:04:47,534 --> 00:04:48,577
Looks like it.

78
00:04:48,702 --> 00:04:50,370
- Is that from a needle?
- Uh, little bigger.

79
00:04:50,704 --> 00:04:52,039
Could be from an IV line.

80
00:04:52,414 --> 00:04:55,292
{\an8}Why would he put an IV In her?
Uh, he's not poisoning them.

81
00:04:55,417 --> 00:04:58,462
{\an8}I don't think he was putting anything in.
More likely, he was taking something out.

82
00:04:58,670 --> 00:05:00,422
{\an8}Could be right. Position the body correctly

83
00:05:00,547 --> 00:05:02,299
{\an8}you can take out a cup or more
of blood with an IV.

84
00:05:02,716 --> 00:05:06,345
{\an8}So he kills them, rips out a fingernail
and takes a cup of blood.

85
00:05:09,306 --> 00:05:11,225
{\an8}And we're making every possible effort.

86
00:05:12,434 --> 00:05:14,520
{\an8}Thanks. All right, thanks for calling.

87
00:05:16,855 --> 00:05:19,483
Everyone and his sister wants to know
when we're making an arrest.

88
00:05:20,442 --> 00:05:22,653
{\an8}Right. This is Rick Tork
from the Santa Fe office.

89
00:05:22,778 --> 00:05:24,154
{\an8}He's gonna help out
while we're short-handed.

90
00:05:24,279 --> 00:05:25,322
{\an8}Hey.

91
00:05:25,447 --> 00:05:27,074
{\an8}Dennis Abbott. Thanks for coming.

92
00:05:27,366 --> 00:05:29,701
{\an8}- So, how long were you in Santa Fe?
- Uh, just a year.

93
00:05:29,910 --> 00:05:32,162
{\an8}I started out CBI, made the jump
to the federal side

94
00:05:32,287 --> 00:05:34,790
{\an8}- about the same time as Cho.
- And he's worked with Jane before.

95
00:05:35,290 --> 00:05:37,167
- Enough to know the score.
- And what's that?

96
00:05:37,960 --> 00:05:39,211
He'll never tell you what he's up to.

97
00:05:39,503 --> 00:05:41,129
Whatever he does,
you'll look like an idiot.

98
00:05:41,839 --> 00:05:43,006
And always keep your hand
on your wallet.

99
00:05:43,465 --> 00:05:44,925
{\an8}Well, you do know the man.

100
00:05:46,552 --> 00:05:49,346
{\an8}I appreciate you coming tonight.
This case is blowing up.

101
00:05:49,471 --> 00:05:51,682
{\an8}- I hear you have 10 bodies.
- Yeah, five were found buried

102
00:05:51,807 --> 00:05:53,392
{\an8}killed between two and nine months ago.

103
00:05:53,809 --> 00:05:55,185
{\an8}Two were killed in their car last week

104
00:05:55,310 --> 00:05:57,396
{\an8}Gabriel Osborne and his sister
a few days after that

105
00:05:57,563 --> 00:06:00,566
{\an8}- and the woman today.
- Wow. Any, uh, physical evidence?

106
00:06:01,066 --> 00:06:02,359
{\an8}Just the bullets...
they match

107
00:06:02,484 --> 00:06:03,902
but we haven't been able
to trace 'em to a gun.

108
00:06:04,027 --> 00:06:06,113
Tork, I heard you were here.
It's good to see you.

109
00:06:06,363 --> 00:06:08,115
- You, too.
- Anything from the profilers?

110
00:06:08,323 --> 00:06:10,993
{\an8}Uh, they can't find any patterns
in the killings.

111
00:06:11,326 --> 00:06:13,287
{\an8}Uh, the first two victims were homeless men

112
00:06:13,412 --> 00:06:14,788
the third was a prostitute.

113
00:06:14,997 --> 00:06:17,416
{\an8}The next ones
were foreign-exchange students

114
00:06:17,541 --> 00:06:19,418
{\an8}and then the couple in the car.

115
00:06:19,585 --> 00:06:22,254
{\an8}There's no consistency
in age, race, or gender.

116
00:06:22,379 --> 00:06:25,799
{\an8}I don't think this is about who he killed
so much as what he killed for.

117
00:06:25,924 --> 00:06:27,467
Hey, Tork. Long time, no see.

118
00:06:27,593 --> 00:06:28,844
Do you mean the blood
and the fingernails?

119
00:06:28,969 --> 00:06:31,805
{\an8}Well, fingernails not so much.
I think they're just a gruesome trophy.

120
00:06:31,930 --> 00:06:33,891
{\an8}But the blood he had to work for.

121
00:06:34,016 --> 00:06:35,559
{\an8}He must need it for something.

122
00:06:35,684 --> 00:06:37,686
Did any of the other victims
have puncture wounds?

123
00:06:37,811 --> 00:06:40,856
Uh, the recent ones, yes.
The buried victims, we couldn't tell.

124
00:06:40,981 --> 00:06:42,316
The bodies had decomposed.

125
00:06:42,441 --> 00:06:45,360
I think we can assume he's been taking
blood samples for some time.

126
00:06:45,652 --> 00:06:48,655
- The question is why.
- There are some theories online.

127
00:06:48,947 --> 00:06:52,117
The most popular theory
is that he's a vampire of some sort.

128
00:06:52,242 --> 00:06:54,536
- Not sure if that's helpful.
- Well, maybe it is.

129
00:06:54,870 --> 00:06:57,122
- Really?
- Well, he is stealing blood from a corpse.

130
00:06:57,247 --> 00:06:58,874
He's gotta be doing something weird
with it.

131
00:06:58,999 --> 00:07:00,375
So, he could be interested in the occult.

132
00:07:00,500 --> 00:07:02,920
He believes in psychics.
That's why he went after Gabriel.

133
00:07:03,378 --> 00:07:04,922
Talk to Austin PD,
see if they have anything

134
00:07:05,047 --> 00:07:06,882
on local cults and nontraditional religions.

135
00:07:07,341 --> 00:07:09,843
Ask Homeland Security if they have
anything useful in their databases.

136
00:07:10,010 --> 00:07:12,429
Well, if he's interested in psychics
Jane should talk to him.

137
00:07:13,847 --> 00:07:16,683
Uh... Not a psychic, dude.

138
00:07:16,808 --> 00:07:17,893
No, but you can fake it, right?

139
00:07:18,936 --> 00:07:20,228
We could feed you to the media

140
00:07:20,437 --> 00:07:22,481
say that you can communicate
with the afterlife

141
00:07:22,606 --> 00:07:24,483
using your spiritual whatever.

142
00:07:24,608 --> 00:07:26,610
If he's really into that,
we can get him to show himself.

143
00:07:27,069 --> 00:07:30,489
The Son of Sam killer sent letters to two
of the writers who wrote about him.

144
00:07:30,781 --> 00:07:32,199
Hey, this kinda thing could really work.

145
00:07:35,160 --> 00:07:36,620
Did I... say something wrong?

146
00:07:36,870 --> 00:07:38,246
Yeah, the last time Jane tried
something like that

147
00:07:38,372 --> 00:07:39,414
it didn't go well.

148
00:07:40,290 --> 00:07:42,542
- Oh, the wife and kid.
- Yeah, the wife and kid.

149
00:07:46,088 --> 00:07:50,801
Hey, uh, I meant to tell you
we got Gabriel's autopsy reports back.

150
00:07:51,843 --> 00:07:55,722
He had oligodendrogliomas...
they're tiny, little tumors in the brain.

151
00:07:55,847 --> 00:07:57,808
According to the coroner,
they can cause seizures

152
00:07:57,933 --> 00:08:00,227
blackouts, or delusional episodes.

153
00:08:00,352 --> 00:08:03,230
Poor kid. No wonder he thought
he was psychic.

154
00:08:03,689 --> 00:08:05,649
There's no such thing as psychics.

155
00:08:06,900 --> 00:08:07,943
No.

156
00:08:09,820 --> 00:08:12,364
I shouldn't have said anything
about the ring. I'm sorry.

157
00:08:12,531 --> 00:08:14,199
- Teresa, please.
- Really, look...

158
00:08:14,324 --> 00:08:15,742
you do what you need to.

159
00:08:16,034 --> 00:08:17,577
I'm okay, I swear.

160
00:08:20,455 --> 00:08:23,041
We just got a call from Austin PD.
They think they have the serial killer.

161
00:08:23,166 --> 00:08:25,168
- Did they arrest him?
- The call said somebody shot him.

162
00:08:34,636 --> 00:08:36,680
- This does not seem right.
- It's a false alarm.

163
00:08:37,014 --> 00:08:40,058
A case of mistaken identity.
This is Sharon Nieto, Austin Homicide.

164
00:08:40,559 --> 00:08:42,144
The dead man is Le Kong Vinh.

165
00:08:42,394 --> 00:08:44,938
According to the neighbors
he goes around collecting recyclables.

166
00:08:45,063 --> 00:08:46,189
The homeowner was asleep

167
00:08:46,314 --> 00:08:48,066
when he heard banging
on the side of the house.

168
00:08:48,233 --> 00:08:49,985
It was Mr. Vinh going through
his garbage

169
00:08:50,277 --> 00:08:51,319
but he didn't know that.

170
00:08:51,445 --> 00:08:54,448
He thought somebody was trying
to break in so he grabs his trusty .38.

171
00:08:54,573 --> 00:08:56,074
Homeowner issued a challenge
through the door.

172
00:08:56,199 --> 00:08:58,326
- Just heard more banging.
- And Vinh didn't speak English.

173
00:08:58,493 --> 00:08:59,536
That's right.

174
00:08:59,703 --> 00:09:01,788
So he fires through the door, calls us

175
00:09:01,913 --> 00:09:03,373
says he shot a serial killer.

176
00:09:03,790 --> 00:09:05,542
- Is that the victim's wife?
- Yeah.

177
00:09:06,001 --> 00:09:07,836
I guess they were collecting
the bottles together.

178
00:09:10,172 --> 00:09:12,883
Are you guys gonna catch
this whack job anytime soon?

179
00:09:13,008 --> 00:09:15,385
People are freaked out.
We're getting calls all day.

180
00:09:15,552 --> 00:09:17,137
Is your department logging
all the calls?

181
00:09:17,429 --> 00:09:18,555
- Sure.
- Then we need that log.

182
00:09:21,600 --> 00:09:22,976
Ah, it's a tough situation.

183
00:09:23,143 --> 00:09:26,063
The city is in a full-on panic,
and we have no solid leads.

184
00:09:27,230 --> 00:09:28,648
Okay, well, uh...

185
00:09:29,900 --> 00:09:32,402
- Do we try Tork's idea?
- What? No.

186
00:09:32,819 --> 00:09:34,404
I don't think that we can rule
anything out.

187
00:09:34,613 --> 00:09:35,655
Boss.

188
00:09:36,281 --> 00:09:38,283
The guy is not hiding bodies anymore.

189
00:09:38,408 --> 00:09:41,620
You know, maybe he's starting to...
to like the attention.

190
00:09:41,745 --> 00:09:44,331
Do you want him to do to Jane
what he did to Gabriel?

191
00:09:44,581 --> 00:09:45,916
Now, you know
we won't let that happen.

192
00:09:46,041 --> 00:09:47,626
- You can't promise that!
- Y-you know what?

193
00:09:47,751 --> 00:09:50,879
I appreciate your spirited defense but it...
it's not necessary.

194
00:09:51,922 --> 00:09:52,964
I'll do it.

195
00:09:54,508 --> 00:09:55,550
Okay.

196
00:09:59,954 --> 00:10:01,623
{\an8}"According to state forestry officials"

197
00:10:01,748 --> 00:10:02,790
{\an8}"once the bear was tranquilized"

198
00:10:02,916 --> 00:10:04,792
"he was relocated to a wilderness area."

199
00:10:05,585 --> 00:10:07,462
"And now an update
from our AccuWeather desk."

200
00:10:07,629 --> 00:10:11,049
I'm gonna say this one last time.
You don't have to do this.

201
00:10:11,216 --> 00:10:12,258
I know that.

202
00:10:12,675 --> 00:10:15,595
Coming up, a psychic
who's working with the FBI.

203
00:10:15,762 --> 00:10:17,680
You're watching Austin Today.
Stay with us.

204
00:10:18,139 --> 00:10:19,599
We're out. Back in 60.

205
00:10:28,608 --> 00:10:29,651
Oh, you've done this before?

206
00:10:31,069 --> 00:10:32,111
Yep.

207
00:10:32,904 --> 00:10:34,822
All right, I'm gonna throw you
a couple easy questions

208
00:10:34,948 --> 00:10:36,282
we'll have some fun,
just keep the ball in the air.

209
00:10:36,491 --> 00:10:37,700
- Sure.
- "Back in 10."

210
00:10:39,285 --> 00:10:42,038
5, 4, 3...

211
00:10:43,915 --> 00:10:46,251
{\an8}"Welcome back to Austin Today.
I'm Dan Glover."

212
00:10:46,376 --> 00:10:49,587
{\an8}"And with me is Patrick Jane
a psychic who works with the FBI."

213
00:10:51,798 --> 00:10:54,217
I'd like to talk about how you're helping
to hunt

214
00:10:54,342 --> 00:10:55,885
for the man
who's believed to have murdered

215
00:10:56,010 --> 00:10:59,013
a number of our local citizens
but first I have to ask...

216
00:10:59,514 --> 00:11:01,474
What is a psychic?
What is it you do?

217
00:11:06,271 --> 00:11:07,313
Patrick?

218
00:11:07,605 --> 00:11:10,191
- Patrick?
- Yeah, Dan, sorry, I was distracted.

219
00:11:10,316 --> 00:11:11,943
Um, there's something on your mind.

220
00:11:12,068 --> 00:11:15,405
Your wife, uh... just had a baby...
a girl, I believe.

221
00:11:16,823 --> 00:11:18,241
- Who told you that?
- You did.

222
00:11:18,950 --> 00:11:23,204
Uh, her, her name begins
with a vowel, A, E, A...

223
00:11:23,329 --> 00:11:26,457
Alexa, uh...
Alexa, right?

224
00:11:26,583 --> 00:11:28,126
That's... right.

225
00:11:29,502 --> 00:11:31,879
- So that's how you do it, huh?
- That's how I do it, Dan.

226
00:11:32,255 --> 00:11:33,673
- Congratulations.
- Thank you.

227
00:11:34,966 --> 00:11:36,009
Your aunt...

228
00:11:38,428 --> 00:11:40,471
passed away about a-a year ago.

229
00:11:41,180 --> 00:11:42,223
18 months.

230
00:11:43,433 --> 00:11:44,601
She used to help people.

231
00:11:45,143 --> 00:11:47,270
- She was a teacher, I think.
- Yes.

232
00:11:47,895 --> 00:11:48,980
Well, a counselor.

233
00:11:50,064 --> 00:11:52,734
We didn't tell him any of this,
swear to God.

234
00:11:53,109 --> 00:11:55,820
She really wants you to be happy
because she loves you...

235
00:11:56,988 --> 00:11:58,031
very much.

236
00:12:02,493 --> 00:12:03,536
That's it.

237
00:12:05,330 --> 00:12:07,999
I-I can't tell you how uncanny this is.

238
00:12:08,124 --> 00:12:09,167
I-I'm shivering.

239
00:12:11,002 --> 00:12:13,296
So, tell us about this case
you're working on with the FBI.

240
00:12:14,964 --> 00:12:17,383
"I'm not a detective.
I don't do police work."

241
00:12:17,508 --> 00:12:20,053
I'm just trying to help my colleagues
understand this man.

242
00:12:20,720 --> 00:12:22,096
"How would you describe him?"

243
00:12:22,722 --> 00:12:25,892
"Well, cautiously, I would say
that he's obviously angry"

244
00:12:26,184 --> 00:12:27,977
probably in a lot of pain

245
00:12:28,645 --> 00:12:32,440
but I think he's trying to get in touch
with someone from the other side.

246
00:12:33,483 --> 00:12:34,609
What makes you say that?

247
00:12:35,818 --> 00:12:36,861
Who isn't?

248
00:12:38,404 --> 00:12:41,616
We have a call from Anna Marie
in Pflugerville.

249
00:12:41,741 --> 00:12:43,159
"Anna Marie, what's your question?"

250
00:12:43,284 --> 00:12:44,327
- Hey.
- "Hi."

251
00:12:44,452 --> 00:12:45,495
What's up?

252
00:12:45,620 --> 00:12:47,288
Uh, Abbott sent me.
You can get outta here.

253
00:12:47,413 --> 00:12:49,499
- I'll take Jane home when he's done.
- Oh, no, I'm okay.

254
00:12:49,624 --> 00:12:52,210
No, forget it. You're beat. Go home.

255
00:12:54,921 --> 00:12:55,963
All right.

256
00:12:56,130 --> 00:12:59,008
"14 months ago. It was shortly after my
mother died."

257
00:12:59,634 --> 00:13:03,429
"Well, I was at home alone,
and I went into the room where my..."

258
00:13:13,314 --> 00:13:15,900
We have another call here from...

259
00:13:17,360 --> 00:13:19,946
Lazarus, welcome to the show.

260
00:13:20,405 --> 00:13:22,699
Lazarus. Interesting name.

261
00:13:23,574 --> 00:13:24,784
"He rose from the dead."

262
00:13:25,993 --> 00:13:27,036
So I hear.

263
00:13:28,037 --> 00:13:29,288
What's your question, Lazarus?

264
00:13:29,664 --> 00:13:31,958
"What else do you know
about the man the FBI is hunting?"

265
00:13:32,834 --> 00:13:34,919
Well, I can't tell you everything
I know.

266
00:13:35,420 --> 00:13:38,005
- "Why not?"
- Well, it's an ongoing investigation.

267
00:13:38,131 --> 00:13:40,633
The case is still open.
Why are you interested?

268
00:13:40,883 --> 00:13:42,510
Do you have information on the man?

269
00:13:42,844 --> 00:13:45,304
- "You're the one who knows everything."
- I never said that.

270
00:13:45,513 --> 00:13:48,266
"No, but you claim to be
in contact with his spirit."

271
00:13:48,391 --> 00:13:50,601
- Boss, you hearing this?
- Yes, we are.

272
00:13:51,352 --> 00:13:52,854
Wylie, how long until you trace
the call?

273
00:13:52,979 --> 00:13:54,021
I'm gonna need another minute.

274
00:13:54,605 --> 00:13:56,524
Make sure Jane keeps him
talking, okay?

275
00:13:56,941 --> 00:13:58,735
"If you're not, why would the police
want your help?"

276
00:14:00,069 --> 00:14:03,281
I get the feeling that you know more
about this case than you're saying.

277
00:14:03,823 --> 00:14:05,950
If that's so, you should probably share.

278
00:14:06,701 --> 00:14:07,744
"Why?"

279
00:14:07,952 --> 00:14:09,120
So we can catch him.

280
00:14:09,871 --> 00:14:11,122
"What if I don't want him caught?"

281
00:14:11,914 --> 00:14:13,166
Oh, why would you feel that way?

282
00:14:13,583 --> 00:14:15,668
"I spoke to someone like you
once before."

283
00:14:16,753 --> 00:14:17,795
Really? Who?

284
00:14:18,379 --> 00:14:19,964
"He was a complete fake."

285
00:14:20,131 --> 00:14:21,758
"You could practically see it
written on him."

286
00:14:24,010 --> 00:14:25,887
We didn't release
what was written on Gabriel's body.

287
00:14:26,012 --> 00:14:27,680
Nobody knows that except us
and the killer.

288
00:14:28,306 --> 00:14:29,348
That's our guy.

289
00:14:29,849 --> 00:14:32,059
That's our guy.
Uh, what's that address?

290
00:14:32,268 --> 00:14:33,936
- Hmm, interesting.
- What?

291
00:14:34,061 --> 00:14:35,146
He's not calling from a cellphone.

292
00:14:35,271 --> 00:14:36,898
He's calling from a landline...
normal phone.

293
00:14:37,398 --> 00:14:38,733
- Okay, that's the address, right?
- Yeah.

294
00:14:39,108 --> 00:14:40,777
Call downstairs. We need backup.

295
00:14:43,112 --> 00:14:45,281
When we left, you suggested
that you dealt

296
00:14:45,406 --> 00:14:48,284
with another psychic
who wasn't on the up-and-up.

297
00:14:48,409 --> 00:14:49,786
Are you a skeptic now?

298
00:14:50,119 --> 00:14:53,498
"No, I believe in spirits very much"

299
00:14:53,748 --> 00:14:55,666
"just not everybody who claims
to be in touch with them."

300
00:14:55,792 --> 00:14:57,168
Any spirits in particular?

301
00:14:57,752 --> 00:14:59,295
"You tell me. Who haunts you?"

302
00:15:00,129 --> 00:15:01,547
Me? Uh, nobody.

303
00:15:06,636 --> 00:15:08,054
"There must be spirits in your life."

304
00:15:08,471 --> 00:15:10,389
Well, fortunately,
they leave me alone.

305
00:15:33,579 --> 00:15:36,666
You still haven't told me whose spirit
you're trying to connect with.

306
00:15:36,791 --> 00:15:39,168
- "Have to go now. Bye."
- Hold on.

307
00:15:40,211 --> 00:15:41,254
Lazarus?

308
00:15:42,630 --> 00:15:43,673
Hello?

309
00:15:44,966 --> 00:15:46,759
Seems the caller has gone.

310
00:15:47,093 --> 00:15:49,220
We're gonna take a minute
for a station ID.

311
00:15:49,345 --> 00:15:52,557
We'll be right back
with Night Talk on KPQC.

312
00:15:56,435 --> 00:15:58,187
Abbott, what's happening?

313
00:15:58,354 --> 00:16:00,356
Something's wrong. He's not here.

314
00:16:00,690 --> 00:16:02,900
He rigged the phone.
We don't know where he is.

315
00:16:03,150 --> 00:16:05,778
"I don't know what he's doing,
but I don't like it."

316
00:16:06,028 --> 00:16:07,989
You and Tork get out of there
and head back to the office.

317
00:16:08,114 --> 00:16:09,323
- "We'll meet you there."
- Okay.

318
00:16:12,034 --> 00:16:13,870
- Cho called. He said...
- Yeah, I heard. Let's go.

319
00:16:14,620 --> 00:16:16,414
Hey, we're doing a show.
Hey!

320
00:16:18,541 --> 00:16:20,459
What happened to you?
I was listening. You got caught off.

321
00:16:20,877 --> 00:16:23,045
Yeah, the call was a ruse.
He's planning something.

322
00:16:23,170 --> 00:16:25,756
"You need to get back
to the office as soon as you can."

323
00:16:29,302 --> 00:16:31,178
Did you leave the door
of the Airstream open this morning?

324
00:16:31,387 --> 00:16:33,014
No. Maybe.
W-why?

325
00:16:35,182 --> 00:16:37,143
- It's open.
- "Okay, stop."

326
00:16:37,476 --> 00:16:38,644
Don't go anywhere near it.

327
00:16:38,769 --> 00:16:40,730
Don't do anything
until someone else gets there.

328
00:16:41,022 --> 00:16:42,648
That could take forever.
I'm gonna check it out.

329
00:16:43,524 --> 00:16:45,318
Yeah, fine, but you're not hanging up.

330
00:16:45,443 --> 00:16:46,903
Jane. We have to go.

331
00:16:47,194 --> 00:16:48,237
Just...

332
00:17:02,209 --> 00:17:03,252
Jane.

333
00:17:04,837 --> 00:17:05,880
Teresa, what's going on?

334
00:17:08,925 --> 00:17:11,427
There's nobody in here.
I guess we left it open.

335
00:17:12,386 --> 00:17:14,847
- Okay, get back to the office.
- All right, I'll see you there.

336
00:17:15,848 --> 00:17:16,891
Let's go.

337
00:17:34,305 --> 00:17:35,348
"Thank you for coming in."

338
00:17:35,849 --> 00:17:39,811
An hour and a half ago
two agents were attacked by a man

339
00:17:39,936 --> 00:17:43,273
who we believe is responsible
for 10 murders in the past year.

340
00:17:44,482 --> 00:17:45,525
This man.

341
00:17:46,192 --> 00:17:48,528
Agent Richard Tork is in the hospital.

342
00:17:48,695 --> 00:17:50,280
I've been told that he's gonna be all right.

343
00:17:50,738 --> 00:17:53,533
Patrick Jane, however,
has been abducted by this man

344
00:17:53,658 --> 00:17:55,118
and is still being held.

345
00:17:55,702 --> 00:17:58,997
So as of right now, no one goes home.

346
00:18:00,123 --> 00:18:02,834
No one takes a nap or a coffee break

347
00:18:02,959 --> 00:18:06,337
until Patrick Jane is returned
and this man is arrested.

348
00:18:07,839 --> 00:18:09,382
Agent Cho will have your assignments.

349
00:18:13,136 --> 00:18:15,388
We found the truck parked
a few blocks away.

350
00:18:15,555 --> 00:18:17,390
We assume the suspect
switched vehicles.

351
00:18:17,515 --> 00:18:20,852
All right, we need a team to sweep
security and traffic cameras in the area.

352
00:18:21,019 --> 00:18:22,103
Elias, that's yours.

353
00:18:22,562 --> 00:18:25,607
We also need fingerprint and DNA
evidence from the truck. Merrick.

354
00:18:25,732 --> 00:18:29,736
You warned me.
I didn't listen, and I am sorry.

355
00:18:32,238 --> 00:18:34,157
He could've killed Jane,
but he took him

356
00:18:34,991 --> 00:18:36,576
so that means he wants something

357
00:18:37,243 --> 00:18:40,788
and there is no one better at exploiting
a situation like that than Jane.

358
00:18:42,540 --> 00:18:43,583
I hope you're right.

359
00:19:08,858 --> 00:19:09,901
Water?

360
00:19:12,904 --> 00:19:14,864
- No, thanks.
- Suit yourself.

361
00:19:19,285 --> 00:19:20,328
You know who I am?

362
00:19:22,622 --> 00:19:24,040
- Lazarus.
- That's right.

363
00:19:25,792 --> 00:19:27,001
You expect me to call you that?

364
00:19:27,669 --> 00:19:28,711
Don't be funny.

365
00:19:28,836 --> 00:19:30,338
Well, you're the one that came up
with the name.

366
00:19:42,266 --> 00:19:43,309
Interesting place.

367
00:19:44,477 --> 00:19:45,687
Could do with a little update.

368
00:19:46,688 --> 00:19:48,398
I saw you on TV.

369
00:19:51,859 --> 00:19:53,277
You said you know things...

370
00:19:55,321 --> 00:19:56,614
hear things.

371
00:20:00,618 --> 00:20:01,661
Prove it.

372
00:20:03,454 --> 00:20:04,831
It doesn't work like that.

373
00:20:05,456 --> 00:20:06,499
You did it on TV.

374
00:20:07,417 --> 00:20:08,793
Different circumstances.

375
00:20:10,044 --> 00:20:11,254
You can't just...

376
00:20:12,171 --> 00:20:13,589
you can't just make it happen.

377
00:20:14,924 --> 00:20:16,551
The other one said something like that.

378
00:20:16,676 --> 00:20:18,428
- You know who I mean?
- Sure.

379
00:20:19,303 --> 00:20:21,055
So, I tested him.

380
00:20:21,597 --> 00:20:24,851
He was a liar. Are you a liar?

381
00:20:25,309 --> 00:20:26,352
No.

382
00:20:39,073 --> 00:20:40,116
Prove it.

383
00:20:49,333 --> 00:20:52,712
- Hi.
- Tork, please, go home.

384
00:20:53,087 --> 00:20:54,714
- I'm okay.
- This isn't your fault.

385
00:20:55,089 --> 00:20:56,924
Any of us had been there,
same thing would've happened.

386
00:20:57,216 --> 00:20:59,886
Yeah, but... I was there.

387
00:21:02,221 --> 00:21:03,264
I'll be at my desk.

388
00:21:08,644 --> 00:21:10,354
- I might have something.
- What?

389
00:21:10,688 --> 00:21:12,482
Jane said the killer was probably
doing something weird

390
00:21:12,607 --> 00:21:13,691
with the blood he took, right?

391
00:21:13,816 --> 00:21:16,861
So, I've been looking into local black
magic and occult connections.

392
00:21:16,986 --> 00:21:18,112
- Find anything?
- Too much.

393
00:21:18,237 --> 00:21:20,198
It's hard to find someone
who doesn't sound like a serial killer.

394
00:21:20,323 --> 00:21:23,534
But one place keeps cropping up...
a bookstore called The Grimoire.

395
00:21:23,659 --> 00:21:26,245
- The Grim, what?
- Grimoire. It's a magical textbook.

396
00:21:26,370 --> 00:21:28,539
Yeah, a lot of people interested
in the stuff go there.

397
00:21:28,956 --> 00:21:31,084
Maybe the killer did, too.
It seemed worth checking it.

398
00:21:32,376 --> 00:21:34,087
It's only three miles
from where the bodies were buried.

399
00:21:34,212 --> 00:21:36,714
Wylie, most of Austin is three miles
from where the bodies were buried.

400
00:21:36,839 --> 00:21:38,841
We appreciate the effort,
but it sounds thin

401
00:21:38,966 --> 00:21:40,343
and we don't have the time to waste.

402
00:21:45,681 --> 00:21:46,724
Jane would go.

403
00:21:47,809 --> 00:21:49,852
He'd say, "Do the usual thing,
you get the usual result."

404
00:21:51,062 --> 00:21:52,772
Which, in this case, is him dead.

405
00:21:54,982 --> 00:21:56,692
Okay, Wylie. Let's go check it out.

406
00:22:05,201 --> 00:22:07,120
This is your father's house, not yours.

407
00:22:08,371 --> 00:22:09,539
A spirit tell you that?

408
00:22:10,164 --> 00:22:11,207
No, the furniture.

409
00:22:13,459 --> 00:22:15,253
Your mother died
when you were very young.

410
00:22:15,837 --> 00:22:17,505
You were raised by your father.

411
00:22:19,549 --> 00:22:20,591
He was strict...

412
00:22:22,760 --> 00:22:24,679
But you feel now that you deserved it.

413
00:22:25,638 --> 00:22:28,850
- He was right to punish you.
- Who's telling you that?

414
00:22:30,143 --> 00:22:31,602
It's what I'm getting from you.

415
00:22:32,979 --> 00:22:34,021
What else?

416
00:22:36,774 --> 00:22:38,776
You didn't have any friends
when you were a kid.

417
00:22:40,611 --> 00:22:41,821
You usually ate alone

418
00:22:42,363 --> 00:22:44,031
not because people
wouldn't sit with you

419
00:22:44,157 --> 00:22:48,369
but because you were disgusted
by the sounds they made when they ate.

420
00:22:50,371 --> 00:22:52,915
Sometimes, other people
don't feel real to you.

421
00:22:54,417 --> 00:22:57,211
They're like robots
wearing human skin.

422
00:22:58,546 --> 00:22:59,672
What do I do for a living?

423
00:23:01,257 --> 00:23:02,508
You're an exterminator.

424
00:23:04,969 --> 00:23:06,470
Yet, again, it doesn't feel real.

425
00:23:08,514 --> 00:23:10,850
It's like a movie being projected
on a screen.

426
00:23:13,019 --> 00:23:14,478
That's impressive.

427
00:23:15,479 --> 00:23:16,522
Thank you.

428
00:23:16,981 --> 00:23:19,150
But I don't need to know about me.

429
00:23:19,859 --> 00:23:21,527
I want contact with another.

430
00:23:23,905 --> 00:23:25,489
I don't sense any spirits here.

431
00:23:26,532 --> 00:23:29,452
You're wrong. The spirit is here.

432
00:23:29,577 --> 00:23:31,329
If you don't know that,
then you're a fraud.

433
00:23:31,454 --> 00:23:33,039
- No, I'm not.
- Just the like the other one.

434
00:23:33,164 --> 00:23:36,250
- I'm not a fraud.
- You're a liar and a cheat.

435
00:23:36,959 --> 00:23:38,002
You take it easy.

436
00:23:52,516 --> 00:23:53,559
Hello?

437
00:23:55,645 --> 00:23:57,104
No, ma'am. The job's finished.

438
00:23:58,731 --> 00:24:00,608
No. No, it's...

439
00:24:01,442 --> 00:24:02,485
Okay.

440
00:24:02,860 --> 00:24:04,153
I'll address that. I'll be right over.

441
00:24:08,824 --> 00:24:09,867
I'll be back.

442
00:24:10,576 --> 00:24:11,953
- Hey.
- What?

443
00:24:13,329 --> 00:24:15,539
Uh, I could...
I could use that water.

444
00:24:21,462 --> 00:24:22,505
Thank you.

445
00:25:47,465 --> 00:25:49,967
- Kelis Weir?
- Kee-lis, yes?

446
00:25:50,134 --> 00:25:51,177
We're with the FBI.

447
00:25:51,927 --> 00:25:55,765
Forget it. I'm not collaborating
with religious persecutors.

448
00:25:56,307 --> 00:25:58,559
- What persecutors?
- We just wanna ask some questions.

449
00:25:58,726 --> 00:26:01,354
You say that, then you start in
with your western morality.

450
00:26:01,604 --> 00:26:02,938
Not fooling me twice.

451
00:26:03,439 --> 00:26:04,482
What do you mean?

452
00:26:04,732 --> 00:26:06,734
A while back, some guy
comes in, starts...

453
00:26:07,360 --> 00:26:08,819
asking about Santeria.

454
00:26:09,195 --> 00:26:11,447
I tell him some friends
are performing a ritual.

455
00:26:11,572 --> 00:26:12,823
Oh, he shows up...

456
00:26:13,449 --> 00:26:17,453
with 10 cops, arrests everybody
for animal abuse.

457
00:26:17,578 --> 00:26:20,623
- Animal abuse?
- People cut up a million chickens a day.

458
00:26:20,790 --> 00:26:24,001
They put testicle-sized chunks
in a fryer, call it commerce.

459
00:26:24,126 --> 00:26:25,169
My friends...

460
00:26:26,253 --> 00:26:29,382
use one for an ancient
and sacred ritual

461
00:26:29,715 --> 00:26:30,758
and I go to jail?

462
00:26:31,425 --> 00:26:34,678
Hey, you're just all a bunch
of Judeo-Christian jackbooted thugs

463
00:26:34,804 --> 00:26:37,139
- as far as I'm concerned.
- Wylie, this is a waste of time.

464
00:26:37,264 --> 00:26:39,642
Hold on, hold on, hold on.
Kelis has a point.

465
00:26:39,767 --> 00:26:41,685
- She was duped. That isn't fair.
- Yeah.

466
00:26:43,104 --> 00:26:45,064
- So?
- So, maybe we can help you.

467
00:26:46,065 --> 00:26:47,108
How?

468
00:26:47,233 --> 00:26:49,151
If you talk to us, just answer
some questions

469
00:26:49,276 --> 00:26:51,946
we'll lean on Austin PD to reduce
your charges, maybe drop 'em.

470
00:26:52,071 --> 00:26:53,114
Why would they do that?

471
00:26:53,447 --> 00:26:54,949
The serial-killer case we're working on

472
00:26:55,241 --> 00:26:58,244
the mayor, Austin PD...
they want him in custody fast.

473
00:26:58,369 --> 00:27:00,538
If you help us make the arrest,
they'll owe us

474
00:27:00,663 --> 00:27:01,872
and we can use that to help you.

475
00:27:04,542 --> 00:27:05,584
He's right.

476
00:27:08,129 --> 00:27:09,171
What do you wanna know?

477
00:27:09,380 --> 00:27:11,507
We're looking for someone
who uses blood.

478
00:27:11,632 --> 00:27:13,259
A lotta people do that.
What kinda blood?

479
00:27:13,384 --> 00:27:14,427
Human blood.

480
00:27:15,344 --> 00:27:16,512
Okay, that's different.

481
00:27:17,138 --> 00:27:19,098
Those people do not come in here.

482
00:27:19,223 --> 00:27:20,724
I'm a little too vanilla for them.

483
00:27:20,850 --> 00:27:22,726
- Where do they go?
- The web mostly.

484
00:27:22,852 --> 00:27:25,688
There's a site called Blackmore.
Hardcores, they go there.

485
00:27:25,813 --> 00:27:27,148
I've been looking.
I haven't found that one.

486
00:27:27,273 --> 00:27:29,024
That's because you gotta go
deep web.

487
00:27:29,150 --> 00:27:31,235
You can't even find the site
without the IP.

488
00:27:32,862 --> 00:27:33,904
Can you give that to us?

489
00:27:35,990 --> 00:27:38,284
You're really gonna talk to Austin PD?
You're really gonna help me?

490
00:27:38,534 --> 00:27:39,577
Yes.

491
00:27:42,496 --> 00:27:43,539
Give me a minute.

492
00:27:48,711 --> 00:27:49,753
It's not bad, huh?

493
00:29:00,488 --> 00:29:02,323
The Blackmore site is huge.

494
00:29:02,348 --> 00:29:04,600
It's the eBay of the deeply weird.

495
00:29:04,725 --> 00:29:08,229
There are sections
on vampirism, self-vivisection...

496
00:29:08,354 --> 00:29:09,605
- Self-vivisection?
- Yeah.

497
00:29:09,730 --> 00:29:11,190
- Cutting yourself open.
- Okay.

498
00:29:11,315 --> 00:29:13,192
How does this help us find Jane?

499
00:29:13,568 --> 00:29:16,404
Well... there's also a section
on blood sorcery...

500
00:29:16,571 --> 00:29:18,239
Magical things you can do with blood.

501
00:29:18,364 --> 00:29:20,658
Now, you're supposed to use
your own blood, but...

502
00:29:20,783 --> 00:29:24,412
15 months ago, there was a discussion
on harvesting blood from other people.

503
00:29:24,537 --> 00:29:25,872
About 20 people were involved.

504
00:29:25,997 --> 00:29:27,498
Why would you harvest blood?

505
00:29:27,748 --> 00:29:28,875
Because you needed a lot.

506
00:29:29,041 --> 00:29:31,085
15 months ago...
that was right around the time

507
00:29:31,210 --> 00:29:32,712
our guy made his first kill.

508
00:29:32,837 --> 00:29:34,964
He could be one of those people.
Can we get their names?

509
00:29:35,089 --> 00:29:37,300
Well the screen names they used
are all super protected.

510
00:29:37,425 --> 00:29:40,970
However, I was able to dig one out...
A guy named Alan Saltonstall.

511
00:29:41,095 --> 00:29:42,555
A college professor in San Marcos.

512
00:29:42,680 --> 00:29:43,806
- Let's go pick him up.
- Sure.

513
00:29:45,683 --> 00:29:47,768
- What do they do with the blood?
- A couple of things

514
00:29:47,894 --> 00:29:51,689
but the one that gets the most discussion
is a ritual that binds a spirit.

515
00:29:52,523 --> 00:29:54,275
- Bind. How?
- If you have a corpse

516
00:29:54,400 --> 00:29:56,027
you can bind the spirit of a dead person

517
00:29:56,194 --> 00:29:57,528
by giving blood to their body.

518
00:29:57,778 --> 00:29:58,863
That way, the spirit never leaves.

519
00:31:00,132 --> 00:31:02,593
- Where are we with the search warrant?
- It's on its way to the judge right now.

520
00:31:04,178 --> 00:31:05,513
- Is that Saltonstall?
- Yeah.

521
00:31:05,638 --> 00:31:06,973
Well, why isn't somebody
talking to him?

522
00:31:07,098 --> 00:31:09,267
He requested an attorney.
He's on his way now.

523
00:31:09,392 --> 00:31:11,060
This guy could be torturing
Jane right now.

524
00:31:11,185 --> 00:31:13,062
- We don't have time for this.
- I'm sorry, Lisbon.

525
00:31:13,187 --> 00:31:15,106
- Let me talk to him.
- Look, the guy's lawyering up.

526
00:31:15,982 --> 00:31:17,024
Let me talk to him.

527
00:31:20,278 --> 00:31:21,320
Okay.

528
00:31:29,120 --> 00:31:32,164
I already told him I won't say anything
without my lawyer present.

529
00:31:32,665 --> 00:31:33,708
I don't care.

530
00:31:38,379 --> 00:31:39,422
You're hiding something.

531
00:31:40,673 --> 00:31:41,716
What?

532
00:31:41,841 --> 00:31:43,551
I never would've noticed something
like this before

533
00:31:43,676 --> 00:31:45,636
but I've been working
for a very long time

534
00:31:45,845 --> 00:31:48,139
with somebody who's good
at seeing into people

535
00:31:48,639 --> 00:31:50,308
what they're thinking, feeling.

536
00:31:51,642 --> 00:31:53,352
I can tell there's something
you're worried

537
00:31:53,477 --> 00:31:55,021
we're gonna find out about you.

538
00:31:55,354 --> 00:31:56,647
That's ridiculous!

539
00:31:56,772 --> 00:31:58,983
I'm guessing it has something
to do with the black magic

540
00:31:59,817 --> 00:32:02,486
something violent or sexual,
maybe both.

541
00:32:05,031 --> 00:32:06,699
But judging by how freaked out
you are

542
00:32:06,824 --> 00:32:08,576
I'd say it's something really bad.

543
00:32:08,701 --> 00:32:10,494
I am not freaked out.

544
00:32:10,620 --> 00:32:13,164
And my interests such as
they are, are purely academic.

545
00:32:13,289 --> 00:32:14,915
- I don't know what you think you're doing
- Shut up.

546
00:32:17,251 --> 00:32:19,962
"I don't care what kinda
kinky stuff you're in to."

547
00:32:20,087 --> 00:32:23,174
I have a friend who's in danger
and maybe you can help save him.

548
00:32:23,382 --> 00:32:25,384
It's possible he's being held
by somebody

549
00:32:25,509 --> 00:32:27,094
from that blood group of yours.

550
00:32:27,261 --> 00:32:28,387
I want their names.

551
00:32:28,512 --> 00:32:31,599
I don't know any names.
It's an online community, and...

552
00:32:32,058 --> 00:32:33,392
I shouldn't even be talking to you.

553
00:32:33,684 --> 00:32:36,562
You're lying. I can tell.
You have names.

554
00:32:36,771 --> 00:32:38,022
You've met them, some of them.

555
00:32:41,609 --> 00:32:44,528
I don't think you understand
how important this is to me.

556
00:32:44,987 --> 00:32:47,365
You give me a name, you can walk
out that door right now.

557
00:32:47,490 --> 00:32:50,868
You don't, and I will dig up
every dirty secret you have!

558
00:32:51,327 --> 00:32:53,621
- You'll what?
- I will tell everybody you know...

559
00:32:53,746 --> 00:32:55,623
your co-workers, your friends,
your family.

560
00:32:55,748 --> 00:32:57,291
You are not gonna be able to hide!

561
00:32:58,417 --> 00:32:59,710
Y-you're threatening me?

562
00:33:00,336 --> 00:33:02,046
It's not a threat.
It's a promise.

563
00:33:02,213 --> 00:33:05,341
You-you can't! That's...
that's illegal.

564
00:33:06,050 --> 00:33:08,636
My boss is right back there.
Tell him.

565
00:33:09,095 --> 00:33:11,889
Get me fired. Ruin my career.
I don't care.

566
00:33:13,115 --> 00:33:14,617
I want those names.

567
00:33:25,419 --> 00:33:27,463
He gave me eight names.
He says he can't remember the rest.

568
00:33:27,588 --> 00:33:30,341
- Good work.
- How do we know he's not the killer?

569
00:33:30,549 --> 00:33:31,592
We checked
his credit-card statements.

570
00:33:31,717 --> 00:33:33,177
He was outta the country
for two of the murders.

571
00:33:33,302 --> 00:33:35,596
Okay, we'll go out in pairs,
and I'll text you the names.

572
00:33:35,721 --> 00:33:37,723
Track 'em down. See if they're connected
to the killings.

573
00:33:37,848 --> 00:33:39,975
If you find a live one
let the rest of the team know fast.

574
00:34:05,334 --> 00:34:06,377
Joe.

575
00:34:08,629 --> 00:34:10,256
He's here, your father.

576
00:34:11,382 --> 00:34:12,424
Big Joe.

577
00:34:13,384 --> 00:34:15,511
That's who you wanna get
in touch with, right?

578
00:34:17,304 --> 00:34:22,142
He says thank you for keeping him
for taking care of him.

579
00:34:25,354 --> 00:34:27,815
The passing over was hard,
but now he's good.

580
00:34:28,482 --> 00:34:30,025
His back doesn't hurt anymore.

581
00:34:30,651 --> 00:34:32,403
He feels better now than he ever did

582
00:34:32,528 --> 00:34:34,780
when Dr. Hannigan was feeding him
his meds.

583
00:34:41,412 --> 00:34:43,372
- There's doubt in you.
- No.

584
00:34:44,039 --> 00:34:45,916
- I-I mean...
- Put it aside. If...

585
00:34:46,500 --> 00:34:49,044
if you doubt, then I lose
the connection with him.

586
00:34:49,169 --> 00:34:50,671
I won't be able to communicate
with him.

587
00:34:51,046 --> 00:34:52,089
Okay.

588
00:34:55,384 --> 00:34:57,553
He says there's a lake...

589
00:34:59,138 --> 00:35:02,182
- A lake Rickasee?
- Pickasee.

590
00:35:04,018 --> 00:35:05,060
Pickasee.

591
00:35:06,604 --> 00:35:09,064
He didn't catch a fish that day.
No.

592
00:35:10,149 --> 00:35:13,485
No, you...
you caught a fish, a small one.

593
00:35:16,780 --> 00:35:17,823
Daddy.

594
00:35:18,657 --> 00:35:21,660
He wants to know
why you're keeping him here.

595
00:35:24,955 --> 00:35:26,498
There's something in me...

596
00:35:28,334 --> 00:35:29,376
a voice.

597
00:35:31,045 --> 00:35:33,464
And when it starts, I can't ignore it.

598
00:35:34,214 --> 00:35:37,885
I can't think about anything else
until I go out...

599
00:35:40,012 --> 00:35:41,096
find someone...

600
00:35:44,099 --> 00:35:45,351
And then it goes away again.

601
00:35:47,102 --> 00:35:48,145
For a while.

602
00:35:51,357 --> 00:35:52,900
Is that your voice, Daddy?

603
00:35:54,985 --> 00:35:59,406
Is that you in me?
Are you sending me out?

604
00:36:02,076 --> 00:36:03,243
Am I doing this for you?

605
00:36:06,872 --> 00:36:09,166
- He's saying something.
- What?

606
00:36:10,084 --> 00:36:11,126
Like...

607
00:36:14,505 --> 00:36:15,631
It's not clear.

608
00:36:16,340 --> 00:36:18,258
- It's not.
- No?

609
00:36:19,093 --> 00:36:21,345
Yeah, I'm so...
I'm-I'm sorry. I...

610
00:36:21,929 --> 00:36:22,972
He's...

611
00:36:23,430 --> 00:36:24,473
He's gone.

612
00:36:25,683 --> 00:36:26,725
Get him back.

613
00:36:28,435 --> 00:36:30,270
I can't. I need...
I need...

614
00:36:30,980 --> 00:36:33,232
- An hour.
- Get him back.

615
00:36:33,524 --> 00:36:36,902
I need an hour. I just, I need to...
I need to rest.

616
00:36:37,194 --> 00:36:38,529
This is how this works.

617
00:36:42,199 --> 00:36:44,451
Hey, can I have some
of that gum, please?

618
00:36:49,331 --> 00:36:50,374
Thank you.

619
00:37:41,414 --> 00:37:43,667
We're looking for a man
named Joseph Keller Junior.

620
00:37:43,792 --> 00:37:45,627
According to our records,
his last known address

621
00:37:45,752 --> 00:37:48,213
was in an apartment building
that you manage, Ms. Martinez.

622
00:37:48,463 --> 00:37:51,716
- But then he moved out.
- Yeah, Keller, weird guy.

623
00:37:52,968 --> 00:37:55,095
Yeah, I think he moved
like two years ago.

624
00:37:55,303 --> 00:37:57,013
- Did he leave a forwarding address?
- No.

625
00:37:57,347 --> 00:37:59,516
I think he said something
about his dad being sick.

626
00:37:59,641 --> 00:38:02,435
Can you remember anything else
about him, where he worked?

627
00:38:02,727 --> 00:38:04,187
Some exterminator company.

628
00:38:04,604 --> 00:38:06,064
Do you know the name
of the company or the address?

629
00:38:06,648 --> 00:38:08,900
Maybe...
I think he sent me an e-mail about it

630
00:38:09,234 --> 00:38:10,277
wanted me to hire him.

631
00:38:11,528 --> 00:38:12,570
You want me to look for it?

632
00:38:12,696 --> 00:38:14,572
- That would be wonderful, thank you.
- Okay.

633
00:38:15,949 --> 00:38:16,992
I know it's in here.

634
00:38:22,330 --> 00:38:24,499
While you're looking for that
we're just gonna step outside.

635
00:38:24,666 --> 00:38:25,709
Okay.

636
00:38:27,961 --> 00:38:29,671
- Any news?
- Not yet, sorry.

637
00:38:29,796 --> 00:38:31,631
But I did find out something weird
about Keller.

638
00:38:31,798 --> 00:38:32,841
What?

639
00:38:32,966 --> 00:38:35,302
Not Keller Junior, but his father,
Joseph Keller Senior.

640
00:38:35,635 --> 00:38:38,221
15 years ago, there was a string
of killings in the area.

641
00:38:38,346 --> 00:38:40,181
Local PD took a hard look
at Keller Senior.

642
00:38:40,307 --> 00:38:42,767
Really liked him for them
but they only had a circumstantial case

643
00:38:42,892 --> 00:38:44,769
never found any conclusive
physical evidence.

644
00:38:44,894 --> 00:38:46,396
Keller's father was a serial killer.

645
00:38:46,855 --> 00:38:48,273
- Sounds like it.
- What happened to him?

646
00:38:48,398 --> 00:38:49,566
I don't know. Case went cold.

647
00:38:49,691 --> 00:38:51,234
Two or three years ago, he falls off
the map.

648
00:38:51,401 --> 00:38:53,778
He had a house not too far outta town,
near Lake Pickasee.

649
00:38:53,945 --> 00:38:54,988
You check out the house.

650
00:38:55,113 --> 00:38:56,614
I'll wait until she finds a work address
and head over there.

651
00:38:56,740 --> 00:38:57,782
Good.

652
00:39:06,833 --> 00:39:07,876
It's been an hour.

653
00:39:08,960 --> 00:39:11,004
- He's here.
- He, what?

654
00:39:11,629 --> 00:39:13,298
He came back when you were gone.

655
00:39:13,631 --> 00:39:16,426
He wants to talk to you.
He's in there.

656
00:39:18,762 --> 00:39:20,722
- He wants to talk to me?
- That's right.

657
00:39:21,514 --> 00:39:23,600
If you want answers,
they're in that room.

658
00:39:24,684 --> 00:39:27,771
You can go in or not.
It's up to you.

659
00:39:36,363 --> 00:39:37,405
Do you smell gas?

660
00:39:39,324 --> 00:39:40,367
No.

661
00:40:48,101 --> 00:40:49,144
"Jane?"

662
00:40:49,561 --> 00:40:51,521
"Jane, are you in here?"

663
00:40:56,151 --> 00:40:57,193
Jane?

664
00:40:58,403 --> 00:41:00,196
Are you here?
Jane?

665
00:41:04,617 --> 00:41:06,411
Jane. Hey.

666
00:41:08,746 --> 00:41:10,582
Can you stand up?
Come on. Let's get you up.

667
00:41:11,791 --> 00:41:12,834
Oh, I got you.

668
00:41:16,546 --> 00:41:17,589
Come on.

669
00:41:26,264 --> 00:41:28,641
Don't you ever do that
to me again, ever.

670
00:41:48,495 --> 00:41:49,537
And sign here...

671
00:41:49,996 --> 00:41:51,372
and here...

672
00:41:53,166 --> 00:41:54,751
- And here...
- There.

673
00:41:55,418 --> 00:41:58,546
- And here. Yeah. That's it.
- Okay.

674
00:42:00,173 --> 00:42:01,216
It's all yours.

675
00:42:01,591 --> 00:42:03,593
Now, usually this is where
I hand over the keys

676
00:42:03,718 --> 00:42:05,053
but there aren't any.

677
00:42:06,679 --> 00:42:07,805
- Congratulations.
- Thank you.

678
00:42:08,556 --> 00:42:10,642
- Thank you so much.
- You're very welcome.

679
00:42:12,560 --> 00:42:13,853
- Bye.
- Bye-bye.

680
00:42:46,334 --> 00:42:47,376
"Previously on The Mentalist..."

681
00:42:47,502 --> 00:42:49,629
- "He says his name is Patrick Jane."
- Never met him.

682
00:42:49,754 --> 00:42:51,881
- Did he say why he came in?
- Just that he wants to talk to you.

683
00:42:52,006 --> 00:42:53,049
Mr. Jane!

684
00:42:53,591 --> 00:42:55,676
"Teresa Lisbon, it's nice to meet you."

685
00:42:56,511 --> 00:42:59,263
We always thought that you and Lisbon
would, you know, get together.

686
00:42:59,680 --> 00:43:00,806
Jane and Lisbon, yeah right.

687
00:43:01,015 --> 00:43:03,392
- And voila.
- So you're gonna build us a house?

688
00:43:03,518 --> 00:43:04,894
- It's a start.
- I need to know

689
00:43:05,019 --> 00:43:07,271
- that you're committed to this, to us.
- I am.

690
00:43:07,396 --> 00:43:08,981
Then are you gonna take off
your wedding ring?

691
00:43:09,148 --> 00:43:11,150
I have a guy who's saying things
about the murders.

692
00:43:11,317 --> 00:43:13,152
- Well, what is he saying Wylie?
- He's a psychic.

693
00:43:13,277 --> 00:43:15,112
I saw that the killer's gonna
kill again, tonight.

694
00:43:15,238 --> 00:43:17,615
"Why would the killer care
if Gabriel was a real psychic?"

695
00:43:17,823 --> 00:43:20,826
"He wants one for some reason
and Gabriel didn't pass the test."

696
00:43:20,952 --> 00:43:22,995
"Welcome back to Austin Today.
I'm Dan Glover."

697
00:43:23,120 --> 00:43:26,082
{\an8}"And with me is Patrick Jane,
a psychic who works with the FBI."

698
00:43:26,207 --> 00:43:28,626
{\an8}I'm just trying to help my colleagues
understand this man.

699
00:43:28,751 --> 00:43:32,255
- "How would you describe him?"
- "I would say that he's obviously angry"

700
00:43:32,421 --> 00:43:34,173
"probably in a lot of pain."

701
00:43:34,340 --> 00:43:35,883
Lazarus. Interesting name.

702
00:43:36,092 --> 00:43:37,969
- "He rose from the dead."
- So I hear.

703
00:43:40,429 --> 00:43:44,058
I saw you on TV.
You said you know things.

704
00:43:44,767 --> 00:43:45,810
He's in there.

705
00:43:57,196 --> 00:43:58,906
Jane... Hey.

706
00:44:01,117 --> 00:44:02,535
Can you stand up?

707
00:44:19,635 --> 00:44:21,220
- You Agent Tork?
- Yeah.

708
00:44:21,345 --> 00:44:22,388
You guys done looking around in there?

709
00:44:22,513 --> 00:44:23,848
'Cause we're just sitting
on our hands out here.

710
00:44:24,015 --> 00:44:25,683
There's nothing we could find.
It's a mess in there.

711
00:44:25,808 --> 00:44:30,021
But the structure's sound.
Your people can go in. Have fun.

712
00:44:30,938 --> 00:44:32,106
Thanks.

713
00:44:32,857 --> 00:44:35,067
All right, listen up.

714
00:44:35,192 --> 00:44:38,112
It's been reported there are two bodies
in the basement of this house.

715
00:44:38,237 --> 00:44:41,449
There may also be evidence
pertaining to as many as 10 homicides

716
00:44:41,699 --> 00:44:44,452
committed by the recently deceased
individual known as Lazarus.

717
00:44:44,744 --> 00:44:46,454
Real name Joseph Keller.

718
00:44:46,662 --> 00:44:48,414
We wanna put these cases to bed

719
00:44:48,581 --> 00:44:50,583
so that means break out
the fine-toothed combs.

720
00:44:50,958 --> 00:44:52,293
Let's go.

721
00:45:48,599 --> 00:45:49,934
How's your head?

722
00:45:50,893 --> 00:45:52,353
- Oh, hey.
- Hi.

723
00:45:52,853 --> 00:45:53,896
It's fine.

724
00:45:54,021 --> 00:45:55,981
Ears are still ringing a little
but, uh...

725
00:45:56,857 --> 00:45:58,609
just getting ready for the remodel.

726
00:45:58,818 --> 00:46:01,278
- I brought sandwiches.
- Those are the magic words.

727
00:46:01,445 --> 00:46:02,530
Come with me.

728
00:46:14,375 --> 00:46:17,962
Is it me, or does it seem like
the house slants a little bit to the left?

729
00:46:20,131 --> 00:46:21,507
Optical illusion.

730
00:46:25,136 --> 00:46:26,429
You're not wearing
your wedding ring.

731
00:46:27,430 --> 00:46:28,597
I'm not married.

732
00:46:33,769 --> 00:46:35,896
The ground is slanty,
so it makes the structure

733
00:46:36,021 --> 00:46:38,649
look like it's leaning,
but it is, in fact, not.

734
00:46:39,066 --> 00:46:40,693
It's just an optical illusion.

735
00:46:41,402 --> 00:46:43,571
- Slanty, huh?
- Yeah.

736
00:46:44,530 --> 00:46:46,115
Technical term.

737
00:46:57,418 --> 00:47:00,880
This ring has been with me
for a very long time, and, uh...

738
00:47:03,716 --> 00:47:07,386
it has obvious significance
with my past.

739
00:47:13,100 --> 00:47:14,894
It also represents...

740
00:47:17,396 --> 00:47:18,814
meeting you.

741
00:47:19,398 --> 00:47:22,985
If I didn't have this ring,
I would never have met you.

742
00:47:23,861 --> 00:47:25,738
So in a sense, uh...

743
00:47:27,615 --> 00:47:30,367
it has the potential to represent
my future, as well.

744
00:47:32,912 --> 00:47:36,165
And I-I'm not expecting
you would ever wear it, but...

745
00:47:36,999 --> 00:47:38,667
I wanna share it with you

746
00:47:39,835 --> 00:47:41,045
and...

747
00:47:42,922 --> 00:47:47,885
I want it to represent our future...
together.

748
00:47:52,640 --> 00:47:54,767
I want you to be my wife.

749
00:47:58,813 --> 00:48:00,314
Will you marry me?

750
00:48:04,443 --> 00:48:05,694
Okay.

751
00:48:06,362 --> 00:48:08,781
- Yes, yes.
- Yes?

752
00:48:09,031 --> 00:48:10,074
Excellent.

753
00:48:11,534 --> 00:48:13,869
I'm glad that's dealt with.
I was a little nervous.

754
00:48:14,119 --> 00:48:15,955
Oh, come on. You knew
I was gonna say yes.

755
00:48:16,288 --> 00:48:19,291
No, even after all these years,
you're still a mystery to me.

756
00:48:19,416 --> 00:48:21,752
- I am?
- Thank you.

757
00:48:40,477 --> 00:48:42,437
Hey, guys, how's the Lazarus case going?

758
00:48:42,563 --> 00:48:44,106
Keller's house is being processed
right now.

759
00:48:44,231 --> 00:48:46,441
Tork's on the scene.
We're just squaring away the paperwork.

760
00:48:46,567 --> 00:48:49,152
Oh, good. Good, good, good.
All right.

761
00:48:50,320 --> 00:48:51,947
Do you guys need anything? Can I help?

762
00:48:52,239 --> 00:48:54,157
Mm... No, not really.

763
00:48:55,242 --> 00:48:58,078
Look, you know, old job's over.

764
00:48:58,245 --> 00:49:01,540
New job hasn't begun. You know,
I'm just spinning my wheels here.

765
00:49:02,708 --> 00:49:04,084
- Hey.
- Hey, guys.

766
00:49:05,085 --> 00:49:09,506
So, um... we wanted you
to be the first to know.

767
00:49:10,257 --> 00:49:12,217
Um... yeah.

768
00:49:13,260 --> 00:49:14,803
We're getting married.

769
00:49:14,970 --> 00:49:16,513
Hey!

770
00:49:17,431 --> 00:49:18,849
- I told you.
- No, you didn't.

771
00:49:19,266 --> 00:49:21,310
{\an8}- Congratulations.
- Oh, man!

772
00:49:21,602 --> 00:49:22,644
{\an8}- That's wonderful.
- That's awesome.

773
00:49:22,769 --> 00:49:23,812
{\an8}- Thank you.
- When's the big day?

774
00:49:23,937 --> 00:49:26,773
{\an8}Eh, no big day.
I don't want any wedding fuss.

775
00:49:26,899 --> 00:49:30,152
Oh, we're just gonna slip away quietly
in the next couple of days.

776
00:49:31,445 --> 00:49:32,487
{\an8}All right.

777
00:49:35,115 --> 00:49:39,411
"It's not unusual to be loved
by anyone"

778
00:49:40,120 --> 00:49:43,707
{\an8}"it's not unusual to have fun
with anyone"

779
00:49:45,542 --> 00:49:48,879
{\an8}"But when I see you
hanging around with anyone"

780
00:49:50,881 --> 00:49:54,051
{\an8}"It's not unusual to see me cry"

781
00:49:55,594 --> 00:49:56,678
"I wanna die"

782
00:50:00,223 --> 00:50:02,059
{\an8}- "Hi. How are you?"
- "Good. How are you?"

783
00:50:02,184 --> 00:50:03,226
{\an8}"Good."

784
00:50:04,353 --> 00:50:08,690
{\an8}"But when I see you out
and about, it's such a crime"

785
00:50:10,359 --> 00:50:12,986
{\an8}"If you should ever wanna be
loved by anyone"

786
00:50:13,111 --> 00:50:14,655
{\an8}- Thank you. Have a nice day.
- Thank you.

787
00:50:15,280 --> 00:50:18,909
"It's not unusual, it happens every day"

788
00:50:19,076 --> 00:50:20,911
Oh, my lord. Sir?

789
00:50:21,995 --> 00:50:23,038
{\an8}I'm good.

790
00:50:24,539 --> 00:50:26,667
That darn barbecue, I swear.

791
00:50:32,839 --> 00:50:35,050
These are two for one, right?

792
00:50:38,470 --> 00:50:41,223
{\an8}- "Hey-hey! Hey!"
- "That's awesome!"

793
00:50:41,598 --> 00:50:43,517
"Hey, even this guy's happy
about it, right?"

794
00:50:43,642 --> 00:50:44,685
"Yeah, congrats."

795
00:50:45,560 --> 00:50:48,105
{\an8}- Oh, hi! Hey!
- "Hey."

796
00:50:48,397 --> 00:50:50,524
{\an8}- "Congratulations!"
- "Somebody went number two."

797
00:50:50,983 --> 00:50:52,567
- Thanks.
- "Yeah. All right."

798
00:50:52,693 --> 00:50:54,820
"So, anyway, did you tell uh--
did you tell Tommy yet?"

799
00:50:54,945 --> 00:50:56,738
{\an8}Eh, he's chasing a bail jumper
in Alaska.

800
00:50:56,863 --> 00:50:57,948
{\an8}I left him a message.

801
00:50:58,198 --> 00:50:59,449
{\an8}"Eh, well, you snooze, you lose."

802
00:50:59,574 --> 00:51:01,284
{\an8}"We're gonna miss him
at the bachelor party, though."

803
00:51:01,410 --> 00:51:03,036
{\an8}There is no bachelor party.

804
00:51:03,203 --> 00:51:04,746
{\an8}We're getting married
the day after tomorrow

805
00:51:04,871 --> 00:51:07,124
{\an8}just me and Jane
and the Justice of the Peace.

806
00:51:07,249 --> 00:51:08,792
{\an8}No big wedding, no guests.

807
00:51:11,420 --> 00:51:13,714
{\an8}"But... family, right?"

808
00:51:13,839 --> 00:51:15,507
- "Yeah, family."
- "Yeah."

809
00:51:15,632 --> 00:51:18,218
{\an8}No, it's just us.
We wanna get married quietly.

810
00:51:18,468 --> 00:51:20,721
"Well, so, we'll be quiet.
But we're gonna be there, T."

811
00:51:20,846 --> 00:51:22,597
- "I mean, no argument."
- "Hey, Stan, hold it."

812
00:51:22,764 --> 00:51:25,434
"It's her deal, her choice.
You know, she wants to do it that way"

813
00:51:25,559 --> 00:51:28,478
{\an8}- "then let her do it."
- "What are you saying, you mook?"

814
00:51:28,603 --> 00:51:29,646
{\an8}Guys, come on!

815
00:51:29,896 --> 00:51:31,481
"If we're not there, Mom's gonna spin
in her grave"

816
00:51:31,606 --> 00:51:33,108
- "like a freaking crankshaft."
- "Oh, my God."

817
00:51:33,233 --> 00:51:35,318
"She'll be crying for shame
that our sister, our only sister--"

818
00:51:35,444 --> 00:51:38,864
{\an8}"Oh, would you can it, please, Stan?
Teresa just said she don't us there."

819
00:51:38,989 --> 00:51:40,991
{\an8}"Why would you wanna be there
if she doesn't want us there?"

820
00:51:41,116 --> 00:51:43,201
- "I mean--"
- "You're a sad, bitter man, Jimmy Lisbon."

821
00:51:43,410 --> 00:51:45,954
- "Well, I-I smile through it."
- "Don't you ever--"

822
00:51:46,079 --> 00:51:47,664
- "I smile through the sadness."
- "Stop it. He's doing it again."

823
00:51:47,789 --> 00:51:49,291
- "I got stronger, though."
- "Ever since he was a little kid--"

824
00:51:49,624 --> 00:51:52,377
- "It's just-- it cuts to the airflow!"
- "Yeah."

825
00:52:19,279 --> 00:52:21,198
- Don't worry.
- Don't worry about what?

826
00:52:21,323 --> 00:52:22,532
You're worried that I'm gonna be upset

827
00:52:22,657 --> 00:52:24,951
because you invited your brothers
to our marriage.

828
00:52:25,077 --> 00:52:26,661
- How did you know that?
- When we're married

829
00:52:26,787 --> 00:52:28,622
do you think you might stop
asking that question?

830
00:52:28,747 --> 00:52:31,124
- It's okay, isn't it?
- They're family.

831
00:52:31,249 --> 00:52:33,418
Thank you. It means a lot to them.

832
00:52:33,543 --> 00:52:34,586
Of course.

833
00:52:37,089 --> 00:52:39,716
Since my brothers are coming
it feels funny

834
00:52:39,841 --> 00:52:42,219
not to invite just a couple
of members from the team.

835
00:52:43,595 --> 00:52:45,013
No, no. You know what? You're right.

836
00:52:45,138 --> 00:52:47,599
We should keep it small.
Small. Just my brothers.

837
00:52:47,849 --> 00:52:49,810
Eh, fine. Invite away.

838
00:52:50,393 --> 00:52:53,480
We're gonna need a few more guests
just to dilute the alcohol content.

839
00:52:53,605 --> 00:52:55,482
- Thank you.
- Just three or four, though.

840
00:52:56,316 --> 00:52:57,526
Where do we draw the line?

841
00:52:57,651 --> 00:52:59,861
Well, that's why we decided
not to invite anyone.

842
00:52:59,986 --> 00:53:02,697
I know. I know. I'm sorry. It's just--
here we are.

843
00:53:02,823 --> 00:53:04,741
- Here we are.
- What?

844
00:53:06,701 --> 00:53:09,121
Oh, look, I'm just gonna surrender
to fate, all right?

845
00:53:09,246 --> 00:53:11,957
So be it.
Big, huge, massive wedding.

846
00:53:12,207 --> 00:53:16,962
No, just 8 or 9 very close friends
at the courthouse-- 9 or 10

847
00:53:17,087 --> 00:53:19,381
and then we can go
to O'Malley's bar afterwards.

848
00:53:19,714 --> 00:53:21,299
12 tops.

849
00:53:21,967 --> 00:53:23,718
Or we could go to a restaurant.
No big deal.

850
00:53:23,844 --> 00:53:25,137
It's not like we're hiring a caterer.

851
00:53:25,262 --> 00:53:28,682
- We don't have a gift registry or anything.
- Sure. Okay.

852
00:53:29,057 --> 00:53:31,143
- Where are you going?
- Well, I have to get you a ring.

853
00:53:31,268 --> 00:53:34,229
- I already have one.
- That is for us.

854
00:53:34,604 --> 00:53:36,356
You need one for you.

855
00:53:36,481 --> 00:53:37,899
- I do?
- You do.

856
00:53:38,567 --> 00:53:40,152
All right, well, shouldn't I come
with you?

857
00:53:40,277 --> 00:53:41,361
Isn't that how you're supposed
to do it?

858
00:53:41,486 --> 00:53:43,905
No, I think we'll waste time bickering.
Besides, I have better taste.

859
00:53:44,072 --> 00:53:45,365
- You think you do.
- You'll see.

860
00:53:46,491 --> 00:53:48,785
- N-nothing too gauche.
- Bye!

861
00:53:50,495 --> 00:53:51,955
- Hey, boss.
- Hey.

862
00:53:53,123 --> 00:53:55,375
The less I have to do,
the more coffee I drink.

863
00:53:55,667 --> 00:53:58,378
So, do you and Lena wanna come
and watch us get married?

864
00:53:58,587 --> 00:54:02,591
Oh. Uh, Lena went to
a trade conference in Prague

865
00:54:02,799 --> 00:54:05,302
but, uh, you know, I'd be honored.

866
00:54:05,635 --> 00:54:06,845
I thought you guys
weren't having any guests.

867
00:54:06,970 --> 00:54:08,513
Well, we kind of changed our minds.

868
00:54:08,638 --> 00:54:11,141
It's just gonna be a few people--
a dozen, 15.

869
00:54:11,266 --> 00:54:13,059
All right. I'm there.
Where and when?

870
00:54:13,185 --> 00:54:14,603
We don't know yet.
It's nothing fancy.

871
00:54:14,728 --> 00:54:17,480
Oh, well, you have to have it
at our house. I insist.

872
00:54:17,772 --> 00:54:19,566
We have the perfect spot
for a casual wedding.

873
00:54:19,691 --> 00:54:20,734
Really?

874
00:54:21,067 --> 00:54:22,235
I'd be thrilled.

875
00:54:22,569 --> 00:54:23,987
That is so nice of you.

876
00:54:31,912 --> 00:54:33,830
- What's up?
- Some surprise, huh?

877
00:54:34,623 --> 00:54:36,499
I didn't see the wedding thing coming.

878
00:54:37,375 --> 00:54:38,460
It wasn't that hard to guess.

879
00:54:44,591 --> 00:54:46,551
- Something on your mind?
- No.

880
00:54:50,513 --> 00:54:51,806
Actually, yes.

881
00:54:52,724 --> 00:54:55,143
Someone might get in touch with you
about me requesting a transfer.

882
00:54:55,268 --> 00:54:56,978
I just wanted you to hear it
from me first.

883
00:54:57,103 --> 00:54:58,396
- A transfer where?
- Salt Lake.

884
00:54:58,605 --> 00:55:00,398
Office there is starting
a cyber-crime initiative.

885
00:55:00,523 --> 00:55:01,566
They're looking for people.

886
00:55:01,691 --> 00:55:04,444
It's desk work,
but it's more my speed, I think.

887
00:55:08,615 --> 00:55:11,243
Uh, let's face it, I didn't do that well
when we were going after Keller.

888
00:55:11,368 --> 00:55:14,913
It's not easy being in the bullpen.
Michelle's desk is right there, and...

889
00:55:15,914 --> 00:55:17,958
Anyway, I think a change of pace
would be good.

890
00:55:18,541 --> 00:55:20,001
Plus, you're gonna be rebuilding
the team.

891
00:55:20,126 --> 00:55:21,586
This'll pretty much
give you a blank slate.

892
00:55:22,379 --> 00:55:24,172
- Come here.
- What?

893
00:55:24,756 --> 00:55:25,924
Come here.

894
00:55:31,054 --> 00:55:32,847
- Stop feeling sorry for yourself.
- No, I'm not.

895
00:55:32,973 --> 00:55:34,140
You are.

896
00:55:34,432 --> 00:55:36,768
You made some mistakes going
after Keller? Welcome to the club.

897
00:55:37,519 --> 00:55:39,187
I bat 300 on a good day.

898
00:55:41,106 --> 00:55:42,357
You miss Vega.

899
00:55:43,316 --> 00:55:44,567
Now remember who she was.

900
00:55:45,402 --> 00:55:47,737
She'd never run away from a challenge
like this and neither should you.

901
00:55:51,366 --> 00:55:52,450
And you're right.

902
00:55:53,159 --> 00:55:56,121
I have to rebuild the team and I wanna
start with people that I know and trust.

903
00:55:56,997 --> 00:55:59,499
- So stick around.
- Or what, you'll hit me again?

904
00:56:01,126 --> 00:56:02,335
I'm asking you to stay, Wylie.

905
00:56:07,632 --> 00:56:10,176
- Okay.
- Okay, good.

906
00:56:12,262 --> 00:56:13,346
Check in with Tork.

907
00:56:13,471 --> 00:56:14,556
I wanna know what's going on
at the house.

908
00:56:14,681 --> 00:56:16,349
Sure. And Cho...

909
00:56:19,311 --> 00:56:21,313
- Thanks.
- No problem.

910
00:56:25,908 --> 00:56:28,161
This is the ring we sent you
a picture of.

911
00:56:28,286 --> 00:56:29,454
It was my grandmother's.

912
00:56:29,579 --> 00:56:31,372
Anne's dad gave it
to me to propose with.

913
00:56:31,497 --> 00:56:34,667
Which is sweet, but it's not
really me, you know?

914
00:56:34,792 --> 00:56:36,794
So we thought maybe we could
take the diamond out

915
00:56:36,919 --> 00:56:38,463
put it in a necklace or something.

916
00:56:38,838 --> 00:56:40,882
Of course. Uh, may I--
may I see it?

917
00:56:41,007 --> 00:56:42,050
Oh, yeah.

918
00:56:45,762 --> 00:56:46,929
Uh, let me get my loupe.

919
00:56:47,055 --> 00:56:48,806
We'll just need to take
a closer look at the stone.

920
00:56:49,182 --> 00:56:50,224
Excuse me, sir.

921
00:56:50,350 --> 00:56:51,809
I'm helping another customer
right now, sir.

922
00:56:51,976 --> 00:56:53,728
FBI--
give 'em back their ring right now

923
00:56:53,853 --> 00:56:55,438
or I will be forced to shoot you.

924
00:56:56,522 --> 00:56:58,149
Don't worry. Just kidding.

925
00:56:58,316 --> 00:56:59,567
I don't even carry a real gun.

926
00:56:59,692 --> 00:57:01,152
I have a lotta close friends
that do, though.

927
00:57:01,319 --> 00:57:03,279
- What's happening?
- All will be revealed.

928
00:57:03,404 --> 00:57:05,948
- Their ring is in your right hand.
- Uh, sir, you've made a mistake.

929
00:57:06,074 --> 00:57:08,493
- We've got the ring right here.
- Uh, that's a replica.

930
00:57:08,618 --> 00:57:09,661
A... replica?

931
00:57:09,786 --> 00:57:13,039
He did a French drop to swap
the valuable ring with a cheap replica.

932
00:57:13,164 --> 00:57:15,708
French drop is a sleight-of-hand move.
Not important.

933
00:57:15,917 --> 00:57:18,169
That ring never belonged
to your grandmother

934
00:57:18,294 --> 00:57:19,837
and it's not a real diamond.

935
00:57:20,380 --> 00:57:22,006
- Is that true?
- Of course not.

936
00:57:22,173 --> 00:57:24,092
He would study the ring
that he just gave you

937
00:57:24,258 --> 00:57:27,679
then break the sad news that
your grandma's ring is a phony

938
00:57:28,012 --> 00:57:29,138
and you'd be none the wiser.

939
00:57:29,597 --> 00:57:30,640
This is insane.

940
00:57:30,765 --> 00:57:32,975
Then you won't mind opening up
your right hand, will you?

941
00:57:35,812 --> 00:57:37,522
Open up your right hand, please, sir.

942
00:57:39,941 --> 00:57:40,983
Holy moly.

943
00:57:41,109 --> 00:57:43,569
Well, thank you for your assistance, folks.
I'll take it from here.

944
00:57:44,821 --> 00:57:47,198
Don't worry, ma'am.
The real ring is in your hand.

945
00:57:47,657 --> 00:57:49,200
- Good day to you.
- Thank you.

946
00:57:49,325 --> 00:57:50,368
My pleasure.

947
00:57:52,662 --> 00:57:55,873
So, my crooked friend,
today is your lucky day.

948
00:57:55,998 --> 00:57:57,458
- Is it?
- Well, on a normal day

949
00:57:57,583 --> 00:58:00,169
you'd be off to the pokey now
but as it happens...

950
00:58:01,212 --> 00:58:02,755
I'm in the market for a diamond ring.

951
00:58:05,633 --> 00:58:07,468
So show me
your very best selection, please.

952
00:58:07,593 --> 00:58:11,472
And, sir, if I see any glass...

953
00:58:12,098 --> 00:58:13,558
the cuffs will come out.

954
00:58:15,059 --> 00:58:16,644
Nothing too gauche.

955
00:58:24,694 --> 00:58:25,737
What's up?

956
00:58:25,862 --> 00:58:26,988
Tork just called in from the crime scene.

957
00:58:27,113 --> 00:58:28,489
No intact corpses in the basement

958
00:58:28,614 --> 00:58:30,950
but a lotta body parts,
badly burned and fragmented.

959
00:58:31,325 --> 00:58:33,870
Have them rush the DNA tests.
Pull some strings if you have to.

960
00:58:34,746 --> 00:58:35,788
Why the rush?

961
00:58:36,080 --> 00:58:37,415
Still got a lotta media interest.

962
00:58:37,540 --> 00:58:39,459
The bosses wanna be able
to announce we got the guy.

963
00:58:39,959 --> 00:58:42,211
For that, we need a coroner's report,
so let's get on it.

964
00:58:42,378 --> 00:58:43,421
Okay, right away.

965
00:58:45,965 --> 00:58:48,134
- Hey, did Abbott give you the news?
- Hey.

966
00:58:48,259 --> 00:58:49,844
We're having a real wedding
at his house.

967
00:58:50,219 --> 00:58:51,804
- He did.
- You're gonna be there, right?

968
00:58:51,929 --> 00:58:52,972
Of course.

969
00:58:53,181 --> 00:58:55,349
I could use your help with something
if you're not too busy.

970
00:58:55,641 --> 00:58:56,684
What's that?

971
00:59:01,898 --> 00:59:03,107
What do you think?

972
00:59:05,985 --> 00:59:07,236
Makes you look short.

973
00:59:17,538 --> 00:59:18,581
Snow cone.

974
00:59:27,048 --> 00:59:28,090
Slutty elf.

975
00:59:29,550 --> 00:59:30,718
You want a simple piece
with clean lines

976
00:59:30,843 --> 00:59:32,345
maybe something vintage
and off-white.

977
00:59:32,678 --> 00:59:33,721
What he said.

978
00:59:35,473 --> 00:59:36,849
Thank you for doing this.

979
00:59:36,974 --> 00:59:38,768
I asked you along
'cause I thought you'd be honest.

980
00:59:38,893 --> 00:59:41,604
I had no idea you were such
a fashion expert.

981
00:59:41,729 --> 00:59:42,772
Not me.

982
00:59:42,897 --> 00:59:44,732
My mom could run up
a designer gown before breakfast.

983
00:59:44,857 --> 00:59:46,192
- Cut her cloth by eye.
- Cool.

984
00:59:46,317 --> 00:59:48,361
My mom had a sewing machine,
but it was always in hock.

985
00:59:50,112 --> 00:59:51,489
She'd be very proud of you.

986
00:59:51,656 --> 00:59:52,782
Looking like this?

987
00:59:53,866 --> 00:59:55,117
Very proud.

988
00:59:56,410 --> 00:59:57,870
Thank you, Kimball.

989
01:00:01,999 --> 01:00:03,459
All right, good night, Wade.

990
01:00:03,584 --> 01:00:06,295
And, uh, tell Shaniqua
I said thanks for the fan mail.

991
01:00:22,186 --> 01:00:23,229
Excuse me.

992
01:00:24,522 --> 01:00:25,606
I-I don't have any change, man.

993
01:00:25,898 --> 01:00:28,860
Hey, hey, hey!
Hey. Okay. Okay. Okay.

994
01:00:29,944 --> 01:00:32,029
Here, look. You can take it.
You can take it. Here.

995
01:00:32,154 --> 01:00:33,364
Get in the car.

996
01:00:35,241 --> 01:00:36,951
Do as I say and you won't get hurt.

997
01:01:04,126 --> 01:01:05,460
Stop the vehicle.

998
01:01:05,919 --> 01:01:07,671
"Very slowly. No one gets hurt."

999
01:01:09,589 --> 01:01:11,967
Put the car in park and get out.

1000
01:01:14,720 --> 01:01:15,762
Easy.

1001
01:01:18,098 --> 01:01:19,141
Easy.

1002
01:01:25,647 --> 01:01:26,732
Give me your phone.

1003
01:01:27,232 --> 01:01:28,275
All right.

1004
01:01:29,693 --> 01:01:30,736
No problems.

1005
01:01:31,987 --> 01:01:33,071
What's the passcode?

1006
01:01:33,697 --> 01:01:34,823
There isn't any.

1007
01:01:37,409 --> 01:01:38,493
Wallet.

1008
01:01:39,703 --> 01:01:41,913
Look, uh, I only got
about 20 bucks in it.

1009
01:01:42,080 --> 01:01:43,373
And, uh...

1010
01:01:44,916 --> 01:01:46,460
Would you let me keep
my driver's license?

1011
01:01:47,044 --> 01:01:49,212
I-I don't wanna have to go
to the DMV.

1012
01:01:49,921 --> 01:01:50,964
Sure.

1013
01:01:57,596 --> 01:01:58,930
Here you go.

1014
01:01:59,681 --> 01:02:00,724
Thanks.

1015
01:02:01,683 --> 01:02:03,018
Thank you.

1016
01:02:04,227 --> 01:02:08,940
No! No! No!
No! No! No!

1017
01:02:38,553 --> 01:02:40,972
- Tork.
- Patrick Jane, please.

1018
01:02:41,098 --> 01:02:42,516
Um, sorry. He's not in.

1019
01:02:42,974 --> 01:02:44,768
This is Dan Glover
from Austin Today.

1020
01:02:44,893 --> 01:02:47,354
I interviewed Jane recently
about this whole Lazarus case.

1021
01:02:47,604 --> 01:02:48,647
Sure. I remember you.

1022
01:02:49,064 --> 01:02:51,358
I just wanna do a quick follow-up.
Is he available?

1023
01:02:51,525 --> 01:02:53,902
I'm afraid, uh, you're gonna have
to wait a few days on that.

1024
01:02:54,027 --> 01:02:55,237
He's outta the office for a while.

1025
01:02:55,362 --> 01:02:57,572
Can you tell me where I can find him?
It'll only take a few moments.

1026
01:02:57,697 --> 01:02:59,783
I'd say he's pretty unfindable
at the moment.

1027
01:02:59,908 --> 01:03:01,243
"He's getting married in a few days."

1028
01:03:01,368 --> 01:03:02,661
- Married?
- Yeah.

1029
01:03:03,328 --> 01:03:05,664
I can, uh, take a message,
tell him you called.

1030
01:03:05,789 --> 01:03:07,999
No, no need.

1031
01:03:08,708 --> 01:03:09,751
Okey-doke.

1032
01:03:16,383 --> 01:03:17,426
Huh.

1033
01:03:27,727 --> 01:03:30,897
If I just remembered how tedious
this aspect of the marriage is

1034
01:03:31,022 --> 01:03:32,441
I might not have asked you.

1035
01:03:32,941 --> 01:03:34,901
No, seriously. I'm only on page two.

1036
01:03:35,110 --> 01:03:37,404
You know, I could just give you
the ring and we could elope.

1037
01:03:37,821 --> 01:03:39,364
Don't be mean. No take-backs.

1038
01:03:41,241 --> 01:03:44,786
I could give you this
and we could be in Fiji by nightfall.

1039
01:03:44,911 --> 01:03:47,497
There are people coming.
We're getting married, damn it.

1040
01:03:47,831 --> 01:03:49,541
- Suit yourself.
- You got a ring?

1041
01:03:49,666 --> 01:03:50,709
Yes, I did.

1042
01:03:51,585 --> 01:03:53,336
- You gonna show it to me?
- You wanna see it?

1043
01:03:53,503 --> 01:03:54,546
Show me.

1044
01:03:56,381 --> 01:03:58,592
I'll take this,
and you'll fill all of this out.

1045
01:04:03,555 --> 01:04:06,099
Oh, my God.
It's not real. You scared me.

1046
01:04:06,224 --> 01:04:07,684
- It's funny.
- Of course it's real.

1047
01:04:08,018 --> 01:04:09,686
- It's real?
- Real.

1048
01:04:12,272 --> 01:04:14,900
Oh, my--
Are you outta your mind?

1049
01:04:15,066 --> 01:04:16,109
You like it?

1050
01:04:16,234 --> 01:04:18,278
Well, it's gorgeous, but it's too much.

1051
01:04:19,154 --> 01:04:20,530
I-I can't accept it.

1052
01:04:21,406 --> 01:04:23,116
You can accept it, and you will.

1053
01:04:23,241 --> 01:04:24,910
It's yours. I want you to have it.

1054
01:04:25,118 --> 01:04:26,828
What is the Justice of the Peace's name?

1055
01:04:26,995 --> 01:04:28,121
Emily Hamilton.

1056
01:04:30,040 --> 01:04:32,042
- Oh, my...
- All right, let's file this sucker.

1057
01:04:33,168 --> 01:04:36,421
All right. We'll need confirmation
that the ceremony's been performed

1058
01:04:36,588 --> 01:04:39,549
within 72 hours, or you will need
to refile.

1059
01:04:40,217 --> 01:04:41,426
Congratulations.

1060
01:04:41,843 --> 01:04:44,221
- Who said romance is dead?
- I can't take this.

1061
01:04:44,387 --> 01:04:45,722
No, not yet you can't.

1062
01:04:46,389 --> 01:04:47,682
Well, at least let me try it on.

1063
01:04:47,807 --> 01:04:49,684
- Not yet.
- We don't even know if it fits!

1064
01:04:56,274 --> 01:04:57,692
- Lisbon, hi.
- Yes!

1065
01:04:57,817 --> 01:04:59,569
- Wylie, did we invite you yet?
- No, not yet.

1066
01:04:59,736 --> 01:05:03,073
Well, here it is.
Abbott's house, 12:00 Saturday.

1067
01:05:03,281 --> 01:05:05,367
But try not to spread it around.
We wanna keep it small.

1068
01:05:05,492 --> 01:05:06,701
And I don't wanna hurt
anybody's feelings.

1069
01:05:06,826 --> 01:05:09,371
I got you. Is there a gift registry?

1070
01:05:09,538 --> 01:05:11,790
- Uh, no gifts.
- Is there a trousseau?

1071
01:05:11,915 --> 01:05:14,292
- I don't know. What is that exactly?
- Never mind.

1072
01:05:16,419 --> 01:05:18,088
You're coming back
to work, right? Here?

1073
01:05:18,213 --> 01:05:20,382
Yeah, I think so.

1074
01:05:20,840 --> 01:05:23,677
- Why are you whispering?
- Lisbon, hey.

1075
01:05:24,177 --> 01:05:25,220
Someone's trying to reach you.

1076
01:05:26,846 --> 01:05:27,889
Oh, my God.

1077
01:05:28,390 --> 01:05:29,933
- "Hey, boss."
- "Hi."

1078
01:05:30,517 --> 01:05:33,728
- I'll talk to you guys later, okay?
- It is so good to see you guys.

1079
01:05:33,895 --> 01:05:35,021
"Right back at ya."

1080
01:05:35,188 --> 01:05:38,233
"Well, the news is spreading fast
through the CBI grapevine."

1081
01:05:38,358 --> 01:05:40,026
- "It's true, isn't it?"
- It's true.

1082
01:05:40,402 --> 01:05:42,404
"Oh, well, we had to call
and say congratulations."

1083
01:05:42,862 --> 01:05:45,907
"So, you and Jane, huh?
We always knew."

1084
01:05:46,283 --> 01:05:47,909
"We always knew?
I always knew."

1085
01:05:48,034 --> 01:05:49,077
How are the kids?

1086
01:05:49,244 --> 01:05:51,997
- "Uh, sticky, mostly."
- "The kids are great."

1087
01:05:52,122 --> 01:05:54,749
I know it's short notice, but you guys
have gotta come out for the wedding.

1088
01:05:54,916 --> 01:05:55,959
It's Saturday.

1089
01:05:56,084 --> 01:05:57,711
"Oh, my gosh, of course.
We'd love to."

1090
01:05:57,877 --> 01:06:00,422
"It will take a little child-care juggling
but we can swing it."

1091
01:06:00,589 --> 01:06:02,382
"You know, worst comes to worst
we'll just bring the little monkeys with us."

1092
01:06:02,549 --> 01:06:04,593
- "Keep 'em locked in the rental car."
- "Will not."

1093
01:06:04,759 --> 01:06:06,553
- "I'm kidding."
- "Mommy!"

1094
01:06:06,928 --> 01:06:08,513
"No, but seriously, we wouldn't
miss it for anything."

1095
01:06:09,014 --> 01:06:10,307
"I gotta go. We'll see you soon."

1096
01:06:10,557 --> 01:06:11,891
All right, I'll send you the details.

1097
01:06:12,058 --> 01:06:13,268
"Great. Take care."

1098
01:06:28,033 --> 01:06:30,660
Okay, you guys are all set. It should be
in the mail three to five days.

1099
01:06:31,161 --> 01:06:32,203
Thanks.

1100
01:06:35,540 --> 01:06:37,584
Excuse me. I need to fill out
a marriage license.

1101
01:06:39,628 --> 01:06:41,838
Um, usually there's two of you.

1102
01:06:42,505 --> 01:06:44,299
She's running late. I'll get started.

1103
01:06:44,841 --> 01:06:47,260
Okay, well, uh, paperwork
is in the end tray.

1104
01:06:47,427 --> 01:06:50,096
Just fill that out.
We need both of you here, plus ID.

1105
01:06:50,263 --> 01:06:51,306
I see.

1106
01:06:51,765 --> 01:06:53,308
Will do, thanks.

1107
01:07:07,906 --> 01:07:09,699
City Clerk's office. Please hold.

1108
01:07:10,617 --> 01:07:12,369
Thanks for holding.
Yes, how may I help you?

1109
01:07:13,411 --> 01:07:15,163
No, ma'am. You can't file online.

1110
01:07:16,122 --> 01:07:18,416
Until six, but we're closed
from twelve to one.

1111
01:07:19,125 --> 01:07:20,168
You're welcome.

1112
01:07:26,132 --> 01:07:29,803
Looks like she stood me up.
Bad omen for a wedding, huh?

1113
01:07:39,270 --> 01:07:40,313
Abbott.

1114
01:07:41,773 --> 01:07:42,816
Can I run something by you?

1115
01:07:43,566 --> 01:07:44,609
Yeah, shoot.

1116
01:07:44,943 --> 01:07:47,362
Spot DNA test came back
from the Keller house.

1117
01:07:47,779 --> 01:07:51,700
So far, all the recovered body parts
belong to Joe Senior, none for Junior.

1118
01:07:51,825 --> 01:07:53,451
They found his gun, but not him.

1119
01:07:53,618 --> 01:07:55,912
Oh, damn.

1120
01:07:56,121 --> 01:07:59,207
It could be that he was at the epicenter
of the explosion and was vaporized.

1121
01:07:59,332 --> 01:08:03,086
But there's a strong possibility
that Keller, A.K.A. Lazarus, is still alive.

1122
01:08:03,628 --> 01:08:04,671
Damn.

1123
01:08:04,838 --> 01:08:06,423
I let Austin PD know

1124
01:08:06,548 --> 01:08:08,675
and we're putting out a BOLO
to all the local hospitals.

1125
01:08:09,008 --> 01:08:10,510
Wylie's putting together a KA list

1126
01:08:10,635 --> 01:08:12,178
and I'm gonna have agents set up
shop at all of them.

1127
01:08:12,303 --> 01:08:14,973
- Well, did you put out a wire just in case--
- He runs for the border, yeah.

1128
01:08:17,434 --> 01:08:19,686
All right, well, it seems like
you have everything handled.

1129
01:08:22,897 --> 01:08:24,858
I don't know if I should tell
Jane and Lisbon.

1130
01:08:24,983 --> 01:08:26,443
- Good question.
- Yeah.

1131
01:08:29,821 --> 01:08:30,947
I wouldn't.

1132
01:08:31,489 --> 01:08:33,116
We don't have enough to be sure.

1133
01:08:33,241 --> 01:08:35,326
And, you know, they're
in a good space right now.

1134
01:08:35,452 --> 01:08:38,079
If Lisbon found out
that this case isn't closed

1135
01:08:38,204 --> 01:08:41,082
it's likely that she'll cancel the wedding
and join the hunt.

1136
01:08:41,958 --> 01:08:44,294
Yeah, there's plenty of time
to tell them after.

1137
01:08:45,795 --> 01:08:48,757
But, if he's still alive...

1138
01:08:48,882 --> 01:08:50,425
You know, Keller's unpredictable

1139
01:08:51,426 --> 01:08:53,094
and Jane did try to kill him.

1140
01:08:54,679 --> 01:08:55,889
You know, just in case

1141
01:08:56,014 --> 01:08:58,808
why don't we put some bodies
at the wedding

1142
01:08:58,933 --> 01:09:00,268
just to keep an eye out.

1143
01:09:00,518 --> 01:09:02,312
And it's my house,
so I'll arrange it.

1144
01:09:02,437 --> 01:09:03,480
You sure?

1145
01:09:03,605 --> 01:09:05,690
Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.
It's something to keep me busy.

1146
01:09:06,274 --> 01:09:07,525
Okay, thanks.

1147
01:09:09,027 --> 01:09:10,487
Abbott said it's totally up to you

1148
01:09:10,612 --> 01:09:13,156
but that you'd probably prefer
to hold the ceremony outside

1149
01:09:13,281 --> 01:09:14,991
and there isn't really
a room inside big enough.

1150
01:09:15,241 --> 01:09:16,743
Well, how many people
are we talking about?

1151
01:09:16,868 --> 01:09:18,495
Oh! A lotta people are talking about it.

1152
01:09:19,078 --> 01:09:21,247
Well, we only invited like 15 people.

1153
01:09:21,498 --> 01:09:25,210
Mm... more like 25 or--
I know.

1154
01:09:25,376 --> 01:09:28,463
And I don't think people
are waiting for, like a printed invitation...

1155
01:09:28,588 --> 01:09:30,590
seeing as there isn't one.

1156
01:09:31,174 --> 01:09:33,718
But, hey, on the plus side,
you're popular, girl!

1157
01:09:34,135 --> 01:09:35,595
Is that what all these tables are for?

1158
01:09:35,720 --> 01:09:36,971
Yeah, Abbott thought they'd be useful.

1159
01:09:37,096 --> 01:09:38,223
Don't worry.
He's covering the rental...

1160
01:09:38,973 --> 01:09:40,016
and the bartender...

1161
01:09:40,683 --> 01:09:41,935
and the caterer.

1162
01:09:42,060 --> 01:09:44,437
I guess they're his wedding gift.
I don't know.

1163
01:09:44,604 --> 01:09:45,647
Hey, here's a menu.

1164
01:09:46,064 --> 01:09:48,608
- There's a caterer?
- Yeah. Yeah, it's fine.

1165
01:09:49,067 --> 01:09:51,569
Abbott's loaded.
I mean, look at this house.

1166
01:09:51,736 --> 01:09:53,530
I think his wife cleaned up
in the private sector.

1167
01:09:53,655 --> 01:09:54,739
Wow.

1168
01:09:54,864 --> 01:09:57,492
"Here we are.
Hey, everybody out."

1169
01:09:57,617 --> 01:09:59,410
- Hey, Teresa!
- Hey!

1170
01:09:59,994 --> 01:10:01,371
- We're here!
- Hey-hey!

1171
01:10:01,746 --> 01:10:02,789
T!

1172
01:10:03,873 --> 01:10:06,084
Hi! Wow!

1173
01:10:06,793 --> 01:10:09,838
- You all came! So many people.
- Yeah, hey.

1174
01:10:09,963 --> 01:10:11,840
Sure we came.
We're gonna let our sister down?

1175
01:10:15,009 --> 01:10:16,594
- Congratulations.
- Thanks.

1176
01:10:16,719 --> 01:10:18,471
Yeah, hey, guys, say hi to your
Aunt Teresa, all right?

1177
01:10:18,596 --> 01:10:20,139
- Hi!
- Hi!

1178
01:10:20,306 --> 01:10:23,309
- Who is this?
- Oh, T, this is Lucy, my fiancée.

1179
01:10:23,726 --> 01:10:24,853
Lucy, Teresa.

1180
01:10:24,978 --> 01:10:27,605
I am so freaked out to meet you at last.

1181
01:10:27,772 --> 01:10:30,900
- We're gonna be sisters! Yay!
- Yay!

1182
01:10:31,025 --> 01:10:32,235
It's a long story.

1183
01:10:34,487 --> 01:10:36,990
- So, you're all here. Welcome to Austin.
- Thanks.

1184
01:10:37,115 --> 01:10:38,658
Yeah, it looks like we brought
the weather with us.

1185
01:10:39,075 --> 01:10:40,159
FBI!

1186
01:10:41,035 --> 01:10:43,955
- Sorry, I'm freaking out right now.
- Yeah, we got that.

1187
01:10:44,581 --> 01:10:45,915
- Excuse me?
- You all came.

1188
01:10:46,040 --> 01:10:48,501
- Yeah. Already said that, T.
- Let's go in!

1189
01:10:48,918 --> 01:10:51,546
- Jason! Jason! Come here!
- Yeah! Okay.

1190
01:10:51,880 --> 01:10:54,215
- Congratulations.
- Thank you.

1191
01:11:10,870 --> 01:11:12,163
Uh, excuse me, sir.

1192
01:11:12,372 --> 01:11:13,832
We have an odd coincidence...

1193
01:11:15,208 --> 01:11:17,002
Or not. Maybe.

1194
01:11:17,293 --> 01:11:19,170
Austin PD got a missing-person's report

1195
01:11:19,337 --> 01:11:21,881
on a local television reporter
named Dan Glover.

1196
01:11:22,007 --> 01:11:23,174
The one that interviewed Jane.

1197
01:11:23,299 --> 01:11:26,428
Yeah, left work Thursday night,
hasn't been seen since.

1198
01:11:26,553 --> 01:11:29,639
The weird thing is, he called here
right around the time he was last seen.

1199
01:11:29,764 --> 01:11:32,225
I spoke to him. He said
he wanted to interview Jane again

1200
01:11:32,350 --> 01:11:34,352
and I said he was unavailable
because he was getting...

1201
01:11:35,562 --> 01:11:36,730
married.

1202
01:11:37,647 --> 01:11:39,774
So, you're not even sure
if you spoke to Glover?

1203
01:11:40,150 --> 01:11:42,736
No, I mean, I was certain
at the time.

1204
01:11:42,861 --> 01:11:44,904
Obviously, it was his caller ID
but now--

1205
01:11:45,071 --> 01:11:47,449
So, we have to assume
the killer's alive and looking for Jane.

1206
01:11:48,324 --> 01:11:49,993
How many agents are you gonna have
at the wedding?

1207
01:11:50,452 --> 01:11:53,079
Four, but now I think
we should probably have more.

1208
01:11:53,246 --> 01:11:54,289
At least 10.

1209
01:11:54,414 --> 01:11:55,749
We're gonna need eyes
on the front and backyards

1210
01:11:55,915 --> 01:11:57,167
and the surrounding neighborhoods.

1211
01:11:57,417 --> 01:11:59,627
We should have a chopper on standby
in case we need to pursue.

1212
01:11:59,753 --> 01:12:00,795
Yes, sir.

1213
01:12:00,920 --> 01:12:03,798
But wouldn't it be wiser
to just postpone the wedding?

1214
01:12:04,799 --> 01:12:07,427
Postpone the wedding?
We're the FBI.

1215
01:12:08,303 --> 01:12:10,221
There is that upside.

1216
01:12:10,430 --> 01:12:13,725
We can use the wedding as bait...
kind of.

1217
01:12:16,853 --> 01:12:18,146
I'm gonna go check on that chopper.

1218
01:12:20,774 --> 01:12:22,692
Still think we shouldn't tell
Jane and Lisbon?

1219
01:12:24,319 --> 01:12:25,653
We're the FBI.

1220
01:12:26,196 --> 01:12:28,198
Just like you said, we can handle it.

1221
01:12:34,079 --> 01:12:35,121
Abbott.

1222
01:12:35,872 --> 01:12:36,915
Hey.

1223
01:12:39,751 --> 01:12:42,128
What were you and Cho and Tork
huddled about?

1224
01:12:44,005 --> 01:12:45,173
Nothing special.

1225
01:12:46,174 --> 01:12:47,300
Nothing special
that's keeping you here

1226
01:12:47,467 --> 01:12:49,427
when you could be in Prague
with your lovely wife?

1227
01:12:51,471 --> 01:12:53,598
You know, she doesn't need me around.
I...

1228
01:12:53,932 --> 01:12:55,100
I get in the way.

1229
01:12:55,809 --> 01:12:57,644
You're lying to me.
I won't pursue the point

1230
01:12:57,769 --> 01:13:00,146
because you would tell me
if it was something important.

1231
01:13:00,355 --> 01:13:01,731
Oh, yeah, yeah.
Yeah, of course.

1232
01:13:01,856 --> 01:13:04,400
If-if I thought that it was something
that we couldn't handle.

1233
01:13:05,318 --> 01:13:07,028
You know, um...

1234
01:13:09,906 --> 01:13:11,866
I've been getting some calls about you

1235
01:13:12,075 --> 01:13:14,119
and my bosses wanna know
if you're sticking around.

1236
01:13:14,244 --> 01:13:15,286
That's a good question.

1237
01:13:17,747 --> 01:13:19,165
All right, well, no pressure.

1238
01:13:19,624 --> 01:13:21,126
But if you're going

1239
01:13:21,251 --> 01:13:23,211
there is some legal stuff
that we need to handle

1240
01:13:23,711 --> 01:13:25,547
to expunge that deal that we made.

1241
01:13:26,047 --> 01:13:27,132
The napkin?

1242
01:13:31,678 --> 01:13:33,263
I'm getting married tomorrow.

1243
01:13:34,556 --> 01:13:36,307
Then I'm building a house, and...

1244
01:13:37,225 --> 01:13:40,436
beyond that
I genuinely have no idea.

1245
01:13:41,729 --> 01:13:43,731
And I can't do this job forever

1246
01:13:45,024 --> 01:13:46,776
but it's gonna be tough to give up.

1247
01:13:46,901 --> 01:13:49,195
Yeah, it's hard giving up
making a difference, huh?

1248
01:13:49,404 --> 01:13:51,114
No, everyone makes a difference.

1249
01:13:51,781 --> 01:13:54,325
- Hard to give up the chase.
- Oh, yeah.

1250
01:13:56,119 --> 01:13:57,579
That it is.

1251
01:14:01,124 --> 01:14:04,335
So, you, uh, let me know
when you know.

1252
01:14:04,460 --> 01:14:05,628
I will.

1253
01:14:07,797 --> 01:14:10,258
It has been very good
working with you, Patrick.

1254
01:14:11,050 --> 01:14:12,802
You too, Dennis.

1255
01:14:13,094 --> 01:14:14,929
I really appreciate your honesty.

1256
01:14:15,263 --> 01:14:16,598
I love you for that.

1257
01:14:18,099 --> 01:14:19,184
Thank you.

1258
01:14:28,109 --> 01:14:29,485
Okay, you got me. I was lying.

1259
01:14:29,611 --> 01:14:31,279
There is something
I need to talk to you about.

1260
01:14:48,087 --> 01:14:49,964
- Hey.
- Hi.

1261
01:14:50,465 --> 01:14:51,633
Nice flowers.

1262
01:14:52,842 --> 01:14:54,177
They're centerpieces.

1263
01:14:55,762 --> 01:14:58,598
- It's a Sylvan theme.
- Sylvan theme.

1264
01:14:59,390 --> 01:15:00,934
All right. Cool, I guess.

1265
01:15:01,100 --> 01:15:04,938
How many... people are
actually coming to this thing?

1266
01:15:05,355 --> 01:15:07,065
Nobody knows exactly.

1267
01:15:09,442 --> 01:15:10,568
Okay.

1268
01:15:11,778 --> 01:15:14,614
How did this happen?
This is not what I wanted.

1269
01:15:16,574 --> 01:15:17,951
Well, I like the Sylvan theme.

1270
01:15:18,076 --> 01:15:19,994
We should've just eloped
like you said.

1271
01:15:21,996 --> 01:15:24,165
- What about your family?
- Oh, they wouldn't care.

1272
01:15:24,290 --> 01:15:26,542
I just talked to them at the hotel.
They found a minibar.

1273
01:15:26,668 --> 01:15:29,504
They're like cavemen
arguing over a dead antelope.

1274
01:15:29,629 --> 01:15:31,297
All right, well, uh...

1275
01:15:31,756 --> 01:15:33,883
Let's run, huh?

1276
01:15:34,217 --> 01:15:36,970
We'll tell nobody, just the judge.

1277
01:15:37,262 --> 01:15:40,223
I'll have her meet us
at our little cabin tomorrow morning.

1278
01:15:40,431 --> 01:15:42,350
- The cabin?
- Just us.

1279
01:15:42,976 --> 01:15:44,269
What, you think the judge
would do that?

1280
01:15:44,394 --> 01:15:46,938
Well, sure. I mean, she's driving in
from San Antonio tonight.

1281
01:15:47,063 --> 01:15:48,606
Change of venue makes
no difference to her.

1282
01:15:48,731 --> 01:15:51,859
- Well, what about the witnesses?
- We'll get someone... Park ranger.

1283
01:15:53,820 --> 01:15:55,154
- You know what? Let's do it.
- Yeah.

1284
01:15:55,280 --> 01:15:56,322
- It's our life, damn it.
- Yes.

1285
01:15:56,447 --> 01:15:58,283
- I love you. Thank you.
- I love you, too.

1286
01:15:58,408 --> 01:15:59,492
- Hey, there's a--
- I'm gonna go get my dress

1287
01:15:59,617 --> 01:16:01,160
and I'm gonna go to the Airstream.
I'll meet you there.

1288
01:16:01,327 --> 01:16:04,998
Well, there's another very good reason
why we should elope, all right?

1289
01:16:05,123 --> 01:16:08,293
Keller is apparently still alive
and he's mad at me for some reason.

1290
01:16:09,711 --> 01:16:12,797
- Oh, my God.
- Yeah, so Cho and his people

1291
01:16:12,922 --> 01:16:14,382
are gonna stake out this house.

1292
01:16:14,549 --> 01:16:16,342
When Keller shows up, they'll nab him.

1293
01:16:16,467 --> 01:16:18,136
You were gonna withhold
this information from me?

1294
01:16:18,261 --> 01:16:20,638
You were gonna deprive me
of a guilt-free elopement?

1295
01:16:20,930 --> 01:16:23,057
- I just told you.
- You almost didn't!

1296
01:16:23,349 --> 01:16:25,768
From now on, we need to be
100% honest with each other.

1297
01:16:25,935 --> 01:16:27,770
- I agree with you 100%.
- Okay.

1298
01:16:28,104 --> 01:16:29,814
- Honesty.
- I am gonna go get my dress.

1299
01:16:29,939 --> 01:16:31,774
- Fire up the Airstream.
- You go, girl.

1300
01:16:37,697 --> 01:16:39,741
Hi. Judge Hamilton, Patrick Jane.

1301
01:16:40,074 --> 01:16:42,160
Uh, there's been a change of venue.

1302
01:16:42,952 --> 01:16:45,705
Okay. No problem, Mr. Jane.

1303
01:16:45,830 --> 01:16:49,375
If you just text me the exact address
and perhaps a decent motel nearby.

1304
01:16:49,500 --> 01:16:50,543
I'll see you tomorrow.

1305
01:16:51,294 --> 01:16:52,545
Great. Bye.

1306
01:17:30,291 --> 01:17:31,667
We got four agents on the roof

1307
01:17:31,834 --> 01:17:33,628
five dressed as catering and valet service

1308
01:17:33,961 --> 01:17:35,004
six on the perimeter

1309
01:17:35,129 --> 01:17:37,215
and six undercover mobiles
covering the approach roads.

1310
01:17:38,049 --> 01:17:39,092
When the guests get here

1311
01:17:39,217 --> 01:17:41,344
I'll gather them inside
and explain the situation.

1312
01:17:41,469 --> 01:17:43,805
Most of them are law enforcement
so they'll understand.

1313
01:17:44,847 --> 01:17:45,973
What is it, Wylie?

1314
01:17:46,099 --> 01:17:47,809
Office got a call off the BOLO
from a clerk

1315
01:17:47,934 --> 01:17:49,560
at the South Austin Registry Office.

1316
01:17:49,685 --> 01:17:51,687
A man with extensive burns
came in yesterday

1317
01:17:51,813 --> 01:17:53,231
and pretended to fill out a form.

1318
01:17:53,356 --> 01:17:54,732
The clerk thinks
he may have taken a peek

1319
01:17:54,857 --> 01:17:56,609
at the marriage-license forms
on her desk.

1320
01:17:56,984 --> 01:17:59,112
So that confirms it.
He is coming to the wedding.

1321
01:17:59,362 --> 01:18:01,155
Well, we got it covered.
Why are you so anxious, Wylie?

1322
01:18:01,364 --> 01:18:03,908
I know all the state forms from
when I used to work downtown.

1323
01:18:04,075 --> 01:18:06,577
The marriage-license form
doesn't ask where the wedding is.

1324
01:18:06,702 --> 01:18:09,205
- It just asks who the officiant is.
- Well, that's the judge.

1325
01:18:09,330 --> 01:18:10,373
Yeah.

1326
01:18:51,038 --> 01:18:52,957
- Hey, you.
- Hi.

1327
01:19:00,173 --> 01:19:01,215
Wow.

1328
01:19:02,550 --> 01:19:06,804
Well, no matter what happens,
from this point on

1329
01:19:08,723 --> 01:19:10,475
we have to promise each other that...

1330
01:19:11,309 --> 01:19:13,102
we will always
look on the bright side.

1331
01:19:13,561 --> 01:19:14,687
I promise.

1332
01:19:18,149 --> 01:19:19,192
Me too.

1333
01:20:05,655 --> 01:20:07,490
Freeze! Drop the gun!

1334
01:20:17,708 --> 01:20:20,545
And see how much better things turn out
when you're honest with me?

1335
01:20:20,670 --> 01:20:21,712
Thank you.

1336
01:20:22,421 --> 01:20:23,506
Let's do this.

1337
01:20:24,549 --> 01:20:25,591
No hard feelings.

1338
01:20:34,897 --> 01:20:38,610
Patrick, do you take Teresa to be
your lawful, wedded wife

1339
01:20:38,735 --> 01:20:41,237
to have and to hold
in sickness and health

1340
01:20:41,487 --> 01:20:44,616
for better or for worse,
till death do you part?

1341
01:20:45,658 --> 01:20:47,035
I sure do.

1342
01:20:47,785 --> 01:20:50,079
And, you, Teresa, do you take Patrick

1343
01:20:50,204 --> 01:20:51,914
to be your lawful, wedded husband

1344
01:20:52,040 --> 01:20:54,500
to have and to hold in sickness and health

1345
01:20:54,626 --> 01:20:57,670
for better or for worse,
till death do you part?

1346
01:20:58,129 --> 01:20:59,297
I do.

1347
01:21:00,381 --> 01:21:03,051
Then by the power granted me
by the State of Texas

1348
01:21:03,426 --> 01:21:06,262
I declare you husband and wife.

1349
01:21:07,138 --> 01:21:08,681
You may kiss the bride.

1350
01:21:15,438 --> 01:21:20,526
Ladies and gentlemen,
Patrick and Teresa.

1351
01:21:42,882 --> 01:21:44,634
"Do you remember"

1352
01:21:45,551 --> 01:21:48,054
"The 21st night of September?"

1353
01:21:48,971 --> 01:21:51,891
"Love was changing the minds
of pretenders"

1354
01:21:52,850 --> 01:21:56,604
- "While chasing the clouds away"
- Who else is gonna hug me? Come on!

1355
01:21:58,398 --> 01:22:00,066
"Our hearts were ringing"

1356
01:22:00,316 --> 01:22:03,569
"In the key that our souls were singing"

1357
01:22:04,320 --> 01:22:07,407
"As we danced in the night, remember"

1358
01:22:08,241 --> 01:22:11,786
"How the stars stole the night away?"

1359
01:22:16,249 --> 01:22:18,209
"Say, do you remember"

1360
01:22:20,044 --> 01:22:22,046
"Dancing in September?"

1361
01:22:24,006 --> 01:22:27,677
"Never was a cloudy day"

1362
01:22:44,318 --> 01:22:45,862
"My thoughts are with you"

1363
01:22:46,237 --> 01:22:49,532
"Holding hands with your heart
to see you"

1364
01:22:50,241 --> 01:22:53,119
"Only blue talk and love, remember"

1365
01:22:54,036 --> 01:22:57,206
"How we knew love was here to stay?"

1366
01:22:59,792 --> 01:23:02,587
"Now, December found the love..."

1367
01:23:04,005 --> 01:23:05,047
How you feeling?

1368
01:23:07,091 --> 01:23:08,634
I am so happy.

1369
01:23:09,635 --> 01:23:11,053
Me too.

1370
01:23:13,347 --> 01:23:14,724
Me too.

1371
01:23:18,519 --> 01:23:20,938
There's something I need to tell you.

1372
01:23:32,241 --> 01:23:34,118
No, you're--
you're kidding me?

1373
01:23:34,243 --> 01:23:35,787
I'm not kidding.

1374
01:23:41,250 --> 01:23:42,919
You are?

1375
01:23:44,045 --> 01:23:45,588
I am.

